{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread","id":786516,"title":"Trans Q+A Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-14T22:18:15-08:00","id":786516,"title":"Trans Q+A Thread","content":"So I am going to try an experiment.<br /> <br /> It can be difficult for non-trans people to understand what trans people are dealing with. Or they have questions and don\u2019t want to sift through page after page of discussing hormones, surgery, and suicides. I understand. I also know trying to ask on the Internet can be\u2026unfriendly. An important step toward acceptance is understanding.<br /> <br /> So, I am going to try an experiment I have seen elsewhere. If you have questions for trans people I (and any other trans posters feeling especially masochistic) will try to answer them as best I/we can.<br /> <br /> This does not remove the requirement to respect other posters. Friendly discussion is welcome, aggressive is not. It is, however, more okay to ask certain types of questions here than elsewhere. No one (me included) is required to answer a question we are uncomfortable with. If I dodge a question I will try to be open about it, however. Also, I am doing this in my free time. Depending on my schedule there may be some long pauses in answering, but I will try to get to them.<br /> <br /> Also, and this is very important, we can only really speak for ourselves on a lot of things. There are some attitudes that are shared, and some that are very unique to the person. If I am aware my feelings are vastly different from others I will tell you, but unfortunately one of us can\u2019t answer anything for all of us.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been involved in LGBT online activism for well over a decade, but I have only been out and living as a woman (mostly) for about 6 months. I don\u2019t have decades of experience. But my answers are better than no answers, and hopefully others will chime in as well, though no one is obligated. If you are not trans and want to answer a question, some advocates are well knowledgeable, just be sure you make that clear in your post.<br /> <br /> So if you have questions, go ahead and we will try to answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T22:30:11-08:00","id":786521,"title":"","content":"As you know, I'm very much in support of this idea, and I'll be happy to answer any questions I can as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T03:48:20-08:00","id":786626,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll start by thanking you and all that participate in this for dispelling ignorance, specially being such a personal and sensitive topic.<br /> <br /> So, my first question is, how does a trans person, or better worded, how did you realize that you were indeed trans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T04:00:43-08:00","id":786633,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much for this thread, Baroness Nerak. I hope I don't seem less grateful for it after I've exposed my ignorance like I'm about to do.<br /> <br /> I've done some study into trans issues just to try to better educate myself, but one thing I've never understood is what the discomfort of gender dysphoria feels like. I've heard people say things like how they feel more comfortable playing with [the other gender's toys] as a child, but never how the upset of being gender dysphoric manifests. I don't know if you're actually gender dysphoric (my research suggests you have to experience a specific minimum amount of dysfunction before you can be called dysphoric), but maybe you've at least talked to some people who have, so: Can you tell me what the discomfort of gender dysphoria feels like? Like, is it a physical discomfort like phantom pain is, or a mental unhappiness, or...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T04:10:45-08:00","id":786636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786626#post786626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'll start by thanking you and all that participate in this for dispelling ignorance, specially being such a personal and sensitive topic.<br /> <br /> So, my first question is, how does a trans person, or better worded, how did you realize that you were indeed trans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sentiment seconded heartily, and I'd add:<br /> <br /> Around what age, ballpark, would you say you realized you were trans, or even the much more nebulous &quot;different&quot;?I really appreciate the openness that you're providing for our communal edification, Nerak, Char, and whomever else might decide to be as open. <br /> I'm personally very interested in moments where people seem to genuinely &quot;see&quot; or know themselves for the first time. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I admit, New input is also for logical extrapolation in regards to my self-identification as Otherkin. I understand it doesn't seem to show up or be spoken of, or especially taken as seriously as LGBTQIA issues. I'm cisgendered (I think), but I still deal with feelings of genuinely being in.the &quot;wrong&quot; body, like I'm missing parts that belong on me, and have others others that don't belong or seem misshapen in comparison to how I picture myself.<br /> <br /> ..if this seems irrelevant or insensitive to your offer of answers or the thread in general, I'll take it down. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T08:14:10-08:00","id":786732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786626#post786626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'll start by thanking you and all that participate in this for dispelling ignorance, specially being such a personal and sensitive topic.<br /> <br /> So, my first question is, how does a trans person, or better worded, how did you realize that you were indeed trans?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786636#post786636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sentiment seconded heartily, and I'd add:<br /> <br /> Around what age, ballpark, would you say you realized you were trans, or even the much more nebulous &amp;quot;different&amp;quot;?I really appreciate the openness that you're providing for our communal edification, Nerak, Char, and whomever else might decide to be as open. <br /> I'm personally very interested in moments where people seem to genuinely &amp;quot;see&amp;quot; or know themselves for the first time. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I admit, New input is also for logical extrapolation in regards to my self-identification as Otherkin. I understand it doesn't seem to show up or be spoken of, or especially taken as seriously as LGBTQIA issues. I'm cisgendered (I think), but I still deal with feelings of genuinely being in.the &amp;quot;wrong&amp;quot; body, like I'm missing parts that belong on me, and have others others that don't belong or seem misshapen in comparison to how I picture myself.<br /> <br /> ..if this seems irrelevant or insensitive to your offer of answers or the thread in general, I'll take it down. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, I'm happy to help any way I can! These questions seem fairly related, so I'm going to try to answer them together.<br /> <br /> From a very young young age, like probably kindergarten, I liked imagining myself as a girl. Usually just privately, in my own head, but sometimes it would come out in little ways. Particularly in games of pretend with my friends, I would sometimes want to play as a girl character. For what ever reason, Star Wars was a big one, when ever we played that I would fight to be Princess Leia. I would get very jealous of the clothes girls got to wear but boys didn't, and this was made worse by the fact that it was ok for girls to wear boy clothes but not the other way around. Of course, at that age I didn't really know transgender was a thing, so I just kind of accepted that I was a boy and that's just the way it was.<br /> <br /> As I got older, maybe in middle school, I started to become aware that there were some people who felt they were &quot;born in the wrong body&quot;, and could undergo some vague procedure to change sex. I very seriously considered the possibility that this might have been what I had been feeling, but that particular trans narrative didn't resonate with me. I had never felt like my body was <i>wrong</i> (body dysmorphia), I just felt like it would have been nice if I had been born different. I got the impression that kind of thing was only &quot;for&quot; people who were caused extreme distress by their bodies, and that didn't really match the way I felt.<br /> <br /> In high school, sex Ed, I found out there was a rare hormone imbalance that could cause boys going through puberty to grow breasts. I remember being excited at even a small possibility that such a thing might happen to me, but at the same time being extremely disheartened by the fact that I was pretty much in puberty at the time, and had most likely already &quot;missed my chance&quot;. And still it didn't really click for me that maybe I was trans, because I still had an extremely limited view of what trans actually meant. At one point, my mom actually asked (seemingly out of nowhere, maybe she was picking up on some unconscious signs I was giving off) if I wished I was a girl and reassured me that that would be ok, and she would support me if I wanted to transition, but I told her pretty much what I said earlier in this post: I'm not <i>unhappy</i> as a boy, so it seems like transitioning isn't something I really <i>need</i>.<br /> <br /> It wasn't until college that I started to become aware that the gender spectrum was much broader than just men, women, and people who changed from one to the other. My college was awesome and had gender-neutral housing options for people who for what ever reason felt unsafe in traditionally gendered dorms, which I immediately knew I wanted to apply for. That was the first time I ever got to meet and interact with other openly trans and non-binary people, and it was a pretty life-changing experience. I got more comfortable experimenting with things like shaving more than my face and wearing women's clothing. I learned more about gender theory and the trans spectrum, and I found a term that resonated with the way I feel (genderfluid).<br /> <br /> So, I guess the short version of that would be, I've always felt &quot;different&quot;, but it wasn't until college that I fully understood those feelings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786633#post786633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much for this thread, Baroness Nerak. I hope I don't seem less grateful for it after I've exposed my ignorance like I'm about to do.<br /> <br /> I've done some study into trans issues just to try to better educate myself, but one thing I've never understood is what the discomfort of gender dysphoria feels like. I've heard people say things like how they feel more comfortable playing with [the other gender's toys] as a child, but never how the upset of being gender dysphoric manifests. I don't know if you're actually gender dysphoric (my research suggests you have to experience a specific minimum amount of dysfunction before you can be called dysphoric), but maybe you've at least talked to some people who have, so: Can you tell me what the discomfort of gender dysphoria feels like? Like, is it a physical discomfort like phantom pain is, or a mental unhappiness, or...?</div> </div> </div> </div>This question I don't think I can really answer, because as I explained in more detail above, I've personally never really struggled with gender dysphoria. It's annoying that my body isn't aesthetically the way I would like it to be, but it doesn't cause me serious distress. Of course, I have a pretty weird relationship with my body to begin with, which I've talked about before in the Otherkin thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T08:46:08-08:00","id":786741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786732#post786732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I learned more about gender theory and the trans spectrum, and I found a term that resonated with the way I feel (genderfluid).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may ask a question about that particular passage of your text, could you define genderfluid for me? I'll try to clarify my question and I apologize in advance if I stumble and sound a little rude, that's absolutely not the intention.<br /> <br /> I understand the difference between sex (biological definition of <i>male</i> and <i>female</i>) as well as gender (man and woman) and the case of someone not feeling like their sex and gender are fitting one another (trans).<br /> <br /> Gender fluidity, however, always seemed strange to me. From an outsider point of view, it seems like it's profoundly anchored in the gender-roles of our society and thus would have little-to-no concept in a more accepting (or free) society. Do you think gender-fluidity is based on the concept that men cannot wear robes and women cannot be garbage collectors? (again, broad simplification)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T09:18:46-08:00","id":786753,"title":"","content":"I am impressed and grateful for the fine people who are opening up this thread to try to dispell some ignorance/answer questions about such personal subjects. I'm always amazed at the bravery of anyone LGBTIA that is willing to share their gender identity or sexual orientation online where anyone can find out.<br /> <br /> I too wish to ask what genderfluid and genderqueer mean.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also want to add a addition to what you said, Magnum Opus. Physical sex isn't quite as binary as Western society teaches people. The physical differences mostly fall into two general groupings but still have a continuum; for example some ethnicities of women have facial hair and/or chest hair, some ethnicities of men have little facial hair, body types differ, etc.<br /> <br /> In addition there are people, about 4% (at least in Western countries), who are born intersex. I'm not intersex (AFAIK) but I did a little research about intersexuality for Women's Studies in college. Intersex babies are born with physical, external genitals that are not immediately easy to categorize as either male or female. The male and female genitals and gonads are homologous anatomy, so it's not possible to have both, but it is possible to be in-between for various reasons (including genetic and hormonal). In Western countries such babies are immediately given surgery without even telling their parents. Which is a huge, unethical invasion and done with no consent, and then in addition what happened and how they were born is kept secret from the children and their parents. Which creates some unhappiness and sexual dysfunction for at least some intersex people as they grow up. There is a movement to oppose this now.<br /> <br /> I know less about the gender identities intersex people tend to have, though (if there is any overall tendency).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-15-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T09:37:07-08:00","id":786757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786741#post786741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may ask a question about that particular passage of your text, could you define genderfluid for me? I'll try to clarify my question and I apologize in advance if I stumble and sound a little rude, that's absolutely not the intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only define what it means to me. The terms we use to describe our identities are many and varied, and the reasons one term may resonate with someone over another term are deeply personal. But I can explain why I prefer to identify as genderfluid, and I believe my feelings are not atypical of those who use the term.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786741#post786741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the difference between sex (biological definition of <i>male</i> and <i>female</i>) as well as gender (man and woman) and the case of someone not feeling like their sex and gender are fitting one another (trans).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to push back on this definition just a bit. Sex and gender are both spectrums. Sex is based on largely objective factors, such as anatomy and bio-chemistry, whereas gender is largely culturally defined. The term transgender describes someone who's gender doesn't match the gender that was assigned to them at birth, sex actually doesn't factor into it much, although some transgender people are also uncomfortable with their sex and may chose to undergo some form of transition, sometimes hormonal, sometimes surgical. Ideally this could be described by the term transsexual, but given the historical misuse of that word, and the related slur, it's best to avoid using it unless you identify that way yourself. The reason I prefer the term genderfluid is because I don't sit in one spot on that gender spectrum all the time. I always feel some mix of masculinity and femininity (which, yes, are subjective qualities), but the balance shifts from day to day, sometimes from hour to hour. I can go into more detail if you like, but that's more or less what it means to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786741#post786741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gender fluidity, however, always seemed strange to me. From an outsider point of view, it seems like it's profoundly anchored in the gender-roles of our society and thus would have little-to-no concept in a more accepting (or free) society. Do you think gender-fluidity is based on the concept that men cannot wear robes and women cannot be garbage collectors? (again, broad simplification)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the concept of transgender relies on the concept of gender, which is culturally defined. In a culture that had no concept of gender, there could be no concept of transgender, nor any of the terms that fall under that umbrella. But I've never heard of such a culture in real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-15-2015, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T10:27:33-08:00","id":786788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786753#post786753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too wish to ask what genderfluid and genderqueer mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Genderqueer is a term I experimented with, but ultimately found it didn't suit me. Its a nonspecific catch-all term for people who fall outside the gender binary. Personally, I used it as a transitionary non-label until I found a term that suited me better. Some others use it because they want to identify themselves as nonbinary but don't want to be tied down to any specific label.<br /> <br /> As for genderfluid, I use it because my gender isn't constant, but it doesn't shift between a set number of specific states, like with bigender. Sometimes I think my goatee looks great on me, but I'm more comfortable in a skirt than pants. Sometimes I can't stand my body hair and have to shave it all off. Sometimes I want to present typically male, even though I feel more feminine. Sometimes I think my deep voice sounds awesome, but more often than not I wish it was higher. Most of the time I wish I had breasts. I always prefer to wear makeup, but most days it's more effort than it's worth. I am not bothered by he/him/his pronouns, but I do prefer to be thought of as a woman, so I use she/her/hers with people I'm &quot;out&quot; to. All of these factors and others are in constant flux, so I believe fluid is the most accurate way to describe my gender.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:02:26-08:00","id":786798,"title":"","content":"Wow, this is a great idea guys. I'm a (nominally) straight cis-male, but having friends (and having had roommates) who identify as trans, you tend to see the sort of discomfort and misunderstanding that comes from people outside the community. There's often this stubborn unwillingness to use the proper pronouns or otherwise respect their identity in otherwise tolerant and respectful people.<br /> <br /> So here's a question. In my (admittedly anecdotal) experience, roleplaying games have a tendency to attract a disproportionately high number of trans people. I've always wondered if it might be an especially attractive safe space where people can explore their identities. Have any of you found that tabletop gaming helped you better come to terms with yourself? Was it in any way therapeutic? Would you feel comfortable sharing any stories? Might it be a tool we actively try to use with younger trans people to come to terms with who they are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 12-15-2015, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:40:49-08:00","id":786820,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine wrote <a href=\"http://chaoslife.findchaos.com/agender-agenda\" target=\"_blank\">this excellent comic</a> about being agender. They're currently working on a sequel to it, of sorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:51:26-08:00","id":786827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786798#post786798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's a question. In my (admittedly anecdotal) experience, roleplaying games have a tendency to attract a disproportionately high number of trans people. I've always wondered if it might be an especially attractive safe space where people can explore their identities. Have any of you found that tabletop gaming helped you better come to terms with yourself? Was it in any way therapeutic? Would you feel comfortable sharing any stories? Might it be a tool we actively try to use with younger trans people to come to terms with who they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! I actually played a trans Galloi character in a Requiem LARP in college (for anyone not familiar with Requiem, the Galloi are a Nosferatu bloodline with an ability to make themselves or others appear eerily beautiful and androgynous) as a sort of preliminary trial coming out. I wasn't yet confident enough to be openly trans, but I figured if I could play a character who was proud to display an odd mix of masculine and feminine traits, it would help me build that confidence for real. &quot;Fake it till you make it&quot;, so to speak. It also had the benefit of allowing me to gain experience interacting with <i>characters</i> who were ignorant and even bigoted, while still feeling safe in the knowledge that the <i>players</i> were all good friends of mine who would support me if and when I was ready to come out.<br /> <br /> I was one of <i>three</i> players in that group who later came out as trans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-15-2015, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T12:32:36-08:00","id":786856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786820#post786820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine wrote <a href=\"http://chaoslife.findchaos.com/agender-agenda\" target=\"_blank\">this excellent comic</a> about being agender. They're currently working on a sequel to it, of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure if this is the best place to ask this, but the comic made me realize something. I'm not even sure how to ask this.<br /> <br /> Do people actually think of themselves as a particular gender all the time? Is being a particular gender so ingrained in your thoughts that affects everything you do?<br /> <br /> Because that comic describes me very well, but I never considered myself agendered.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this as &quot;there is no such thing as agendered,&quot; but rather &quot;well, that may explain a lot.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T12:39:13-08:00","id":786861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786856#post786856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people actually think of themselves as a particular gender all the time? Is being a particular gender so ingrained in your thoughts that affects everything you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't <i>always</i> think of myself as a man (because that would be a heavy toll on my cognitive pursszaaaaaaaa-- where was I?) but I do associate with &quot;man&quot; when interacted with, and I am more enclined to do &quot;manly&quot; things than &quot;girly&quot; things (Sewing and Animal Crossing are manly activities, right?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T12:47:36-08:00","id":786867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786861#post786861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't <i>always</i> think of myself as a man (because that would be a heavy toll on my cognitive pursszaaaaaaaa-- where was I?) but I do associate with &quot;man&quot; when interacted with, and I am more enclined to do &quot;manly&quot; things than &quot;girly&quot; things (Sewing and Animal Crossing are manly activities, right?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't divide my activities into Manly and Girly. I play games, read, write, knit, code SQL, curse at linux servers, and waste time on the internet. <br /> <br /> Eh. I need to do more thinking about this. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:02:08-08:00","id":786877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786856#post786856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if this is the best place to ask this, but the comic made me realize something. I'm not even sure how to ask this.<br /> <br /> Do people actually think of themselves as a particular gender all the time? Is being a particular gender so ingrained in your thoughts that affects everything you do?<br /> <br /> Because that comic describes me very well, but I never considered myself agendered.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this as &quot;there is no such thing as agendered,&quot; but rather &quot;well, that may explain a lot.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's different for different people. I think trans people tend to be more conscious of our gender more often than cis people are, due to the fact that we are constantly being misgendered. To use an analogy, I don't usually think about the fact that I'm named Andrew. But if someone calls me Andy, or Drew, or something else that isn't my name, it might irritate me for a moment. Fortunately, I can just correct them: &quot;I prefer Andrew, actually.&quot; &quot;Oh, ok, sorry.&quot; Then we move on. But when you're misgendered, it's not that easy. Imagine everyone always calling you by the wrong name, and when you try to correct them, you get an insistent &quot;you sure look like an Andy to me.&quot; Or an indifferent &quot;Well, it's going to be pretty hard for me to remember that.&quot; Or an agressive &quot;Stop acting like such a special snowflake, your name is Andy and that's all there is to it!&quot; Maybe if you're lucky, a concerned &quot;Oh my god, I'm soooooooo sorry! I can't believe I misnamed you like that, I feel like such a horrible person. I'm not a namophobe, I swear!&quot; ...You'd probably spend a lot more time consciously aware of your name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-15-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:08:09-08:00","id":786880,"title":"","content":"I just got home! Will start replying soon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:37:54-08:00","id":786907,"title":"","content":"A question that is, perhaps surprisingly, game-related...<br /> <br /> When writing Werewolf: th\u200be Forsaken 2e, I included a power called Luna's Embrace that simply allows the werewolf to trivially flip sex at will between male and female. It's a full-body biological swap-over, because Luna is strongly symbolically linked with concepts of change and werewolves are supposed to be excellent shape-shifters. When writing it, I was a bit worried that it might be seen poorly by trans people; I was concerned that it might feel like it trivialises all the stuff that many trans people go through. Obviously, I did a sanity-check with other writers and they said it seemed fine, but I've wanted to know how any trans people in the player base feel about it for a while. Poor choice of power to write up? Ambivalence? Happy that it's there?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:46:31-08:00","id":786916,"title":"","content":"Okay I think this thread has pointed towards the right answer and IanW's friends' comic helped too but I just want to make sure. Your sex is what your body is, physically, while your gender is what you identify as?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:47:25-08:00","id":786917,"title":"","content":"Okay trying to hit everyone. If I did not answer a question, draw my attention to it I will try again I just read the whole thing at once. And feel free to ask for clarification.<br /> <br /> Thorbes: For me it took forever. Sometime long ago I decided I wished I was a girl, but accepted my lot otherwise. I met some really cool people on rpg.net, and last year I went to GenCon and actually interacted with Trans women who were incredibly cool. I agonized about it for almost a year after but finally got started and haven't looked back. So realized I wanted to be a girl was probably late teens early twenties. Deciding to transition? Somewhere around forty. I am also a moron.<br /> <br /> JimB: it's fine, this is a place for questions like that. Frankly, it is mostly an intense feeling of disquiet. It is a feeling my body is not right. I do not suffer huge dysphoria myself outside of facial hair, which the sensations I would attribute to it is disquiet and despair. Feeling my face like that really makes me feel, well, like ripping it off. Feeling like it is wrong and I am doomed. Fortunately, shaving is a simple task, even if I am hyper sensitive about it now. Everyone has something they always notice and think is ugly, whether it is grey hairs or a largish nose. I see any stubble, and I want it to go away NOW.<br /> <br /> AzraelFirestorm: I knew I was different as a child. I did not know how. Realized I was trans? 39. As I told Thorbes realized I wanted to be/should be female? 17 or 18? One thing is I was not exposed really to GLBT stuff till college, so one thing that slowed me down as a teen was lack of interest in men. I enjoyed my attraction to women and did not want it to change. Then I realized in college GLBTs were a thing, but I was never around like any trans persons.<br /> <br /> When I was a teen I had an imaginary girlfriend. She was not someone (generally) I fantasized about sexually. Often, I was not even in it, except to account for the fact that she (of course) needed a man. She was confidant, dark, mysterious, witty\u2026everything I wasn\u2019t. Sexy wasn\u2019t even a big part of it. It was the mystique. I did not realize she wasn\u2019t what I wanted to have; <i>she was what I wanted to be.</i><br /> <br /> Or as a friend pointed out \u201cYou always play female characters, you even play female video game characters, you describe your character\u2019s wardrobes, interests, even favorite foods in detail\u2026and this is a surprise for you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Magnum Opus: I\u2026am not the best person to ask about Genderfluid. Since Charlequin is here I will let them field that.<br /> <br /> Erinys: Like Charlequin, I identified as genderqueer briefly, before I accepted being trans. This does NOT mean genderqueer is a phase. Some people (like me) realized they were queer from a gender perspective before realizing they were trans. Some people absolutely fit genderqueer well.<br /> <br /> Dxanders: Absolutely. Ironically, this both helped me and slowed me down in accepting being trans. It helped because I had spent a lot of time thinking of myself as female (in games) and exploring that. It slowed me down because RPGs helped me cope with being in the closet from myself. Twice a week I was a girl, everyone called me she and by a femineine name, I thought about my clothes and juggled my social schedule. It was not enough, but it kept me sane. I just did not realize I was exploring that part of myself, but when I did start to transition, I realized I knew just what sort of look I wanted for myself, what kind of clothes I liked, etc. So it helped me, even if it slowed me down\u2026and it slowed me down by keeping me sane.<br /> <br /> Wonderandawe: I think of myself as female all the time. It does not usually influence my thoughts \u201cI am a girl so I do this\u201d but it does cross my mind. Mostly what I do I do because it is me. As Charlequein says, though, I think trans people are often more aware of it then cisgender people are. But there are plenty of \u201cX is not manly/ladylike\u201d sorts out there.<br /> <br /> Acrozatarim: Does not bother me. Some people would love gender tourism. From a carnal perspective, experiencing sexual intercourse from \u201cboth sides\u201d has an appeal. So for me no, it is fine. I am never bothered by gender change stuff though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-04-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:50:34-08:00","id":786923,"title":"","content":"Nofather: Generally, yes.<br /> <br /> Of course for trans people it is complicated. For me, my gender is female, my sex at this point I have a mix of male and female traits. My understanding is if you took a blood or saliva sample you would say I was female, or responded to chemical signals. I am not positive but that is my understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:02:28-08:00","id":786932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786907#post786907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question that is, perhaps surprisingly, game-related...<br /> <br /> When writing Werewolf: th\u200be Forsaken 2e, I included a power called Luna's Embrace that simply allows the werewolf to trivially flip sex at will between male and female. It's a full-body biological swap-over, because Luna is strongly symbolically linked with concepts of change and werewolves are supposed to be excellent shape-shifters. When writing it, I was a bit worried that it might be seen poorly by trans people; I was concerned that it might feel like it trivialises all the stuff that many trans people go through. Obviously, I did a sanity-check with other writers and they said it seemed fine, but I've wanted to know how any trans people in the player base feel about it for a while. Poor choice of power to write up? Ambivalence? Happy that it's there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>love</i> Luna's Embrace, thank you so much for including it in the game! So does my partner, who is bigender. Far from trivializing trans struggles, it opens up a new avenue for exploring trans experiences in a world of shapeshifters and spirits. Hpw does a trans man react when he learns he is a werewolf and can use his shape shifting powers to transition in a way that is totally safe, reliable, and functional? What about an ostensibly cis werewolf who is surprised to find they're actually more comfortable in a &quot;female body&quot;? How about a werewolf who views Luna's Embrace the same way as the five forms - just one more shape that is no more or less their true form than Urhan or Dalu? (that's my personal favorite as a player). Are there transphobic Ivory Claws that view Luna's Embrace as shameful? More options for exploring sex and gender in the Chronicles of Darkness is always a good thing in my book. Also, Luna's Embrace is handled much better than Transgression of Attis, which was a valiant but flawed effort, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:03:26-08:00","id":786934,"title":"","content":"Okay thanks, I knew sex wasn't binary but I tend to be a literal person and wasn't completely sure which the words referred to.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a> I'm not trans but I've been really thrilled with the facet as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:15:01-08:00","id":786942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786917#post786917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dxanders: Absolutely. Ironically, this both helped me and slowed me down in accepting being trans. It helped because I had spent a lot of time thinking of myself as female (in games) and exploring that. It slowed me down because RPGs helped me cope with being in the closet from myself. Twice a week I was a girl, everyone called me she and by a femineine name, I thought about my clothes and juggled my social schedule. It was not enough, but it kept me sane. I just did not realize I was exploring that part of myself, but when I did start to transition, I realized I knew just what sort of look I wanted for myself, what kind of clothes I liked, etc. So it helped me, even if it slowed me down\u2026and it slowed me down by keeping me sane.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting. Are there any games in particular that speak out to you as particularly friendly or more positive towards trans and general LGBQT themes, either in terms of how they're designed or the community they tend to draw? (Feel free to jump in as well here, Charlaquin!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:17:51-08:00","id":786944,"title":"","content":"By the way, for anyone who has trouble grokking the gender/sex/sexuality division, here's an infographic that I find <i>incredibly</i> helpful. It's gone through a few revisions, and I don't know if this is the most up-to-date version available, but it communicates the concept extremely well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://itspronouncedmetrosexual.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/Genderbread-Person-3.3.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:27:20-08:00","id":786949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786907#post786907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question that is, perhaps surprisingly, game-related...<br /> <br /> When writing Werewolf: th\u200be Forsaken 2e, I included a power called Luna's Embrace that simply allows the werewolf to trivially flip sex at will between male and female. It's a full-body biological swap-over, because Luna is strongly symbolically linked with concepts of change and werewolves are supposed to be excellent shape-shifters. When writing it, I was a bit worried that it might be seen poorly by trans people; I was concerned that it might feel like it trivialises all the stuff that many trans people go through. Obviously, I did a sanity-check with other writers and they said it seemed fine, but I've wanted to know how any trans people in the player base feel about it for a while. Poor choice of power to write up? Ambivalence? Happy that it's there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I was lukewarm on it. &quot;Sex swap&quot; powers have a tendency to essentialise transness and sex and it does that a fair bit - you can magically become the 'opposite' sex (which presupposes that's that's a meaningful thing, right). This is why I usually prefer not to have marked out powers like this unless there's room to really explore the queer aspects of the power in text. Contrariwise it creates the potential for interesting queer stories about bodies and identities, so that's good. It certainly didn't fill me with Eternal Crusading Rage.<br /> <br /> Nofather: Ish. From certain approaches.<br /> <br /> The danger of this kind of approach is that it tends to be like &quot;oh you're a trans woman, so like, your gender is woman but your sex is male, right?&quot; and that's not a helpful perspective. Or to frame sex as real/objective/physical and gender as social/subjective.<br /> <br /> I think you can usefully distinguish between sex and gender, and talk about sex as being about bodies and gender as being about our social selves, with the understanding that these are a) interlinked and b) <i>both</i> socially constructed. You can look at certain aspects of a person objectively - where are their gonads, what are their gametes like, what are their hormone levels - and decide subjectively that this means they're 'male' or 'female' or 'intersex' (which itself is then generally reinterpreted as 'deviant male'/'deviant female') but those are subjective categories we impose on those bodies, not objective facts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:29:58-08:00","id":786951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crabbadon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786949#post786949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The danger of this kind of approach is that it tends to be like &quot;oh you're a trans woman, so like, your gender is woman but your sex is male, right?&quot; and that's not a helpful perspective. Or to frame sex as real/objective/physical and gender as social/subjective.<br /> <br /> I think you can usefully distinguish between sex and gender, and talk about sex as being about bodies and gender as being about our social selves, with the understanding that these are a) interlinked and b) <i>both</i> socially constructed. You can look at certain aspects of a person objectively - where are their gonads, what are their gametes like, what are their hormone levels - and decide subjectively that this means they're 'male' or 'female' or 'intersex' (which itself is then generally reinterpreted as 'deviant male'/'deviant female') but those are subjective categories we impose on those bodies, not objective facts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotcha, I was more concerned about the definitions of the terms, than labeling anyone with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:44:32-08:00","id":786961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786944#post786944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, for anyone who has trouble grokking the gender/sex/sexuality division, here's an infographic that I find <i>incredibly</i> helpful. It's gone through a few revisions, and I don't know if this is the most up-to-date version available, but it communicates the concept extremely well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was very helpful. I didn't realize gender identity and gender expression was two different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:54:34-08:00","id":786974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786961#post786961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was very helpful. I didn't realize gender identity and gender expression was two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! I'm glad I could help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T15:52:12-08:00","id":787001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786942#post786942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's interesting. Are there any games in particular that speak out to you as particularly friendly or more positive towards trans and general LGBQT themes, either in terms of how they're designed or the community they tend to draw? (Feel free to jump in as well here, Charlaquin!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Honest, non-shill answer: White-Wolf/Onyx Path. It had queer men and women in 1991-2 over 20 years ago. It's kept having them, and not as jokes. Women in control of their bodies, gays, lesbians, bisexual characters...all go all the way back to Vampire: The Masquerade 1e and never went away. Vampire: the Masquerade a bit later also brought Trans characters, and they showed in Scion and Exalted as well (and, of course, other queer types in those games). Other companies since have had good stuff as well, but WW/OP have done a lot for queer visibility and feminism, all the way back to the start. And many of the LGBTQA+s and women I have played with played WW/OP games.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T19:57:45-08:00","id":787102,"title":"","content":"Now I'm curious whether that inclusivity also goes back to the first edition of Ars Magica, or if it first was done with Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T21:57:31-08:00","id":787153,"title":"","content":"I don't have any Ars Magica books to know. You have discovered the bounds of my 1337ness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T03:28:12-08:00","id":787252,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm also transitioning (MtF, 6 months real life, FFS in a month, SRS will be next summer), so I might as well chip in with my experiences.<br /> <br /> My story is actually rather similar to Baroness Nerak's, but there are always differences: I suffered a lot more from denial and gender dysphoria. So, here goes:<br /> <br /> As a child I personally didn't really notice anything different. I was a rather dreamy, introverted kid who was always reading, however. What I do remember was being very conscious of my body. It always needed to be covered, no way my mom could get me in shorts or something like that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this of course got worse during puberty, and like Baroness Nerak, I realized I wanted to be a girl around 17, 18. This hit me very, very hard. It was actually so traumatic, and the desire seemed so impossible to achieve that I suffered a serious breakdown. My mind, in order to protect myself, proceeded to lock my memories of this revelation in a vault, built a castle around it and threw the keys away. This happened in my first year of university, so went largely unobserved by friends and family, who had no clue what was happening to me, except that I was pretty depressed.<br /> <br /> So, life went on in denial, which brings me to the subject of gender dysphoria. I suffered greatly from it, probably because of my denial, but I still find that feeling really hard to put into words. But let's give it another shot: it is an overwhelming sense that something, everything is wrong. Nothing you do can ever alleviate it. And I tried. I tried just about everything. It poisons every aspect of your life until it leaves you hollowed out, left with nothing but quiet despair and the certainty that nothing can ever be right. In the end I just stopped feeling, let's call it emotionally undead. I know, it sounds grim and dramatic. It was. Gender dysphoria is vile, loathsome stuff. I don't wish it on my worst enemy.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, I am very lucky to have survived it. I have my friends to thank for that. But roleplay was equally important. I always played girls, of course. I have to strongly agree with Baroness Nerak here: being a girl for an evening a couple of times per week kept me sane (and alive). But also, I have the feeling that perhaps I could have broken through my denial sooner if I didn't have that outlet. Dunno. <br /> <br /> Odd observation: I felt the dysphoria more acutely when having sex with men than with women. At least with women, one of us was 'right', and I could, in my mind, pretend to be her. How you pull of remaining in denial when you pretend to be the woman you're having sex with, or that all your sexual fantasies involve you being a woman, still amazes me. Anyway, with men the feeling of wrongness, because I wanted to do stuff with them that was plain impossible, because, well, wrong body , was much stronger. As you can imagine, over the years, sex became progressively more difficult. <br /> <br /> For me, it was also at the age of 39 that the dam broke. Now, 41, I am approaching the end of the transition. I fully identify as, and live as a woman and the gender dysphoria is breathing it's last breaths. All is well, and getting better. The hormone treatment has kicked off what I can only describe as a second puberty, which is a rather wild and at times tiring ride, but yay, welcome back emotions! Very, very, extremely impatient for the final surgery though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T06:55:44-08:00","id":787327,"title":"","content":"That was quite enlightening, thanks Angwe.<br /> <br /> Forgive my ignorance but waht does MtF, FFS and SRS stand for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:08:17-08:00","id":787336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=786942#post786942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any games in particular that speak out to you as particularly friendly or more positive towards trans and general LGBQT themes, either in terms of how they're designed or the community they tend to draw? (Feel free to jump in as well here, Charlaquin!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Onyx Path just keeps getting better at this, and they're a company I trust both to start from a good baseline of knowledge and to consult with trans (in particular here) people. That said, I've never seen anyone who puts a scratch on Avery Mcdaldno//Buriedwithoutceremony for consciously designing queer content (and I always recommend the Queer Content sidebar in Monsterhearts for writers and roleplayers, especially cis or het ones)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=787327#post787327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was quite enlightening, thanks Angwe.<br /> <br /> Forgive my ignorance but waht does MtF, FFS and SRS stand for?</div> </div> </div> </div>MtF: Male to Female. Not all trans women/transfeminine people like this term.<br /> FFS: Facial Feminisation Surgery.<br /> SRS: Sex Reassignment Surgery; 'bottom surgery'. <i>Usually</i> refers to vaginoplasty, phalloplasty or metoidioplasty.<br /> <br /> (also I never thought I'd find myself saying this, but I kinda hope we get some transmasculine people speaking up in this thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T08:39:03-08:00","id":787388,"title":"","content":"I was almost sure SRS was that but better safe than sorry, the others I had absolutely no idea. I second your sentiment, crabbadon, but I don't know of any poster that fits the criteria, we'll see.<br /> <br /> So far I can say I have learned a lot already and the tone and mood seems quite aproachable and friendly, so kudos to everyone!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T09:11:57-08:00","id":787420,"title":"","content":"Another common acronym is HRT - hormone replacement therapy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T09:44:19-08:00","id":787450,"title":"","content":"I mean, you could fill a book, innit<br /> <br /> off the top of my head<br /> GIC: Gender identity clinic, in the UK (at least) the tertiary service which provides counselling, HRT consultations, surgery referrals etc. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">and frequently an awful lot of bullshit time-wasting and harrassment</span> to trans patients<br /> GCS: Gender confirmation surgery<br /> GRS: Gender reassignment surgery/genital reconstruction surgery<br /> IPL: intermittent pulse laser, a kind of semi-permanent depilation<br /> T: testosterone<br /> FtM: Female to male<br /> MtX/MtN/FtX/FtN: following that pattern, to X/neuter/neutrois, used variously by genderqueer/non-binary/neutrois people, esp. with regards to physical dysphoria<br /> <br /> ooh do you know what for your actual TLAs I think I'm out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> fewer than I thought<br /> <br /> ofc, certain terms might be received more or less warmly by different people and carry more or less baggage with them too, so take a little care","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T10:14:55-08:00","id":787473,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing, Angwe. I suspect that to some degree for our generation we are sort of typical...with greater openness the past 5 or so years a lot of us are transitioning later in life because it is more out there in a positive way, which is one thing for me with this thread...I hope to educate people in a place that is safe to ask questions, but also maybe if someone like me a couple years ago is here, maybe I can help her.<br /> <br /> I will note about OP that as far as trans persons, I have two books I helped work on currently out (albeit both under my old name) and a third on the way. Now my goal is having my new name in a book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And while I am not outing anyone, there are trans women who have written a lot more than I for the company. Not to mention the large number of other lgbts that have as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-16-2015, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T11:33:32-08:00","id":787525,"title":"","content":"True, the openness and acceptance definitely play a big part. The LBGT community here in Belgium has also been pushing the topic for the last 2 years, with great success. Positive stories in all the magazines, documentaries on tv, the whole works. They have done great work.<br /> <br /> But at least for me, it was also the fact that I was at the right point in my life, with a well-paying job and a stable relationship. We just bought a house and stuff. There was just room for it all to come out without my life imploding. Also, mid-life crisis, I guess? But instead of a sports-car a new body?<br /> <br /> Well, ok, not a sports-car. In that regard, lucky to live in Belgium, I suppose. It still costs plenty of \u20ac's, especially after buying the house, but they don't bankrupt you here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T12:20:39-08:00","id":787555,"title":"","content":"Oh wow Angwe, I am also 41, and also bought a house just before transitioning, and am in a stable relationshiip (though was for awhile). it is getting creepy now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To the thread in general: I prefer questions be out where several trans persons can answer, but if you have something you are embarrassed to ask in public, you can PM me. if you want I can ask the thread your question without attribution, but only will if asked to. I know it can be personal/sensitive. <br /> <br /> Also, as a reminder, if I am not answering something you asked, ask me again, I prolly missed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T13:00:52-08:00","id":787588,"title":"","content":"Hmm...<br /> <br /> Do you have any favorite transgender characters from TV, movies, books, comics? Do you feel there's been improvement in the visibility and representation of trans characters?<br /> Do you think the LGBTAQI community is doing enough to support transgender individuals?<br /> What were your experiences, if any, dealing with nurses, doctors, insurance companies? Do they still require a psychiatrist approval before any hormone therapy or surgery?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T13:29:10-08:00","id":787605,"title":"","content":"Good questions<br /> <br /> Honest answer: I don't feel a huge draw to transgender characters compared to lesbian characters, trans or cis. I do identify well with them, but in terms of favorite characters, that tends to fall toward lesbians/bisexual women (again, trans or cis, just not as defining). Probably because in terms of words to define myself, &quot;lesbian&quot; &quot;woman&quot; and &quot;Queer&quot; and even &quot;Goth&quot; are way ahead of, say, &quot;Transgender' &quot;White&quot; or &quot;North Carolinian.&quot; It's not that I DON'T identify that way, but give me a queer woman and I have a good projection character.<br /> <br /> Depends on the group. Broadly? No. Specifically? Some LGBT groups are AWESOME and go way out of their way to make sure we feel at home. Some are terrible and wish we did not exist, or even see us as a setback to selling Queer folks as normal. And within that, not all trans are treated the same. I am very feminine, honestly moreso than many of my cis friends or hell even my wife. And feminine trans women get more acceptance than butch ones, or gender nonconforming ones (say, a woman with a beard or goatee) so even in a space that welcomes me (who fully embraces the feminine) may be unfriendly to Charlequin. Then you have stuff like tensions over Drag Queens (which leads nearly to knock down drag out fights in some circles) and it gets complicated. Now, most LGBT organizations give lip service to looking out for Trans folks, and some do a better job than others. The HRC for example has a spotty record. But I have also dealt with incredibly accepting LGBT folks. I want us to get along. But then, I have not been burned by cisgendered queer folks. Some trans women who have now have very, very strong opinions on it.<br /> <br /> My experiences with doctors have been mostly positive. My personal physician does not discuss it much but takes it into account and has given me no problems over it. My Cardiologist is...well, I told him, he looked at me, and went on as if I had not said anything. No issues...but not really what I would call acceptance either. I needed a letter to get on HRT, and was lucky a Cis friend asked a queer listserve at her work about a good place to go, and they recommended a wonderful place that was very affirming. I got my letter in one two hours visit. My insurance covers my medicine. For an American, I have it pretty good, though money is very tight and I have to scrimp and save even for laser. I have not even started looking into surgery of any sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-16-2015, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T19:23:21-08:00","id":787776,"title":"","content":"I stalked the good Baroness here from elsewhere; had to, since I haven't been around these forums since they were black and yellow. I hope no one minds me throwing my hat in the ring, but I'm likely to be bored for the rest of the week and I'm hungry for even virtual interaction...and I enjoy answering questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=787588#post787588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...<br /> <br /> Do you have any favorite transgender characters from TV, movies, books, comics? Do you feel there's been improvement in the visibility and representation of trans characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not many, sadly. There wasn't much representation of trans characters to start with, and much of what there was, was downright offensive or just based on such bizarre misunderstandings of what trans experiences are like that I can't empathize with them. The representations that were well done often cast us as victims (thinking of Wanda from Gaiman's &quot;A Game of You&quot; here), which isn't exactly how I'd want to be represented.<br /> <br /> I can still think of a few I like, despite all that. I think my favorite was Brigitte Lin's character in Swordsman II. She was a villain, sure, but a sympathetic one. Also, one of the two romantic interests for Jet Li's character, which I thought was pretty ballsy. I understand that interpreting the character as a trans woman rather than a male eunuch marks a departure of the movie from the book it was based on, but it made the character much more personally interesting to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think the LGBTAQI community is doing enough to support transgender individuals?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all over the map, like Baroness Nerak said. What I am starting to see is a worrying trend of LGBT advocacy groups deciding that now that marriage equality is in, it's time to throw in the towel because, hey, job finished, right? I guess I worry, sometimes, that trans folks will be left to fight on alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What were your experiences, if any, dealing with nurses, doctors, insurance companies? Do they still require a psychiatrist approval before any hormone therapy or surgery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I lie to them as much as I can and interact with them as little as I can.<br /> <br /> That probably seems odd to say, for someone who works in the medical field, but at the same time working in a hospital has left me kind of jaded. Since there's almost no data on medical care for trans patients, I feel like it comes down to a choice between which way I want my medical care to err. I worry that if medical practitioners know I'm trans, they commit the common mistake of cis people in assuming that I'm &quot;biologically male,&quot; and thus judge things like my blood pressure and body fat etc. by cis male standards. Thing is, most of those differences are hormonally governed, and I've been on HRT for quite some time, so they should be judging me by cis female standards. And if they don't, they could give me seriously bad advice, but I don't trust them to do the proper thing on their own recognizance.<br /> <br /> And then, of course, there's the simple respect factor. Receptionists and nurses...regardless of how feminine I was presenting myself (quite feminine, at the time) and the fact that I had my name legally changed, before I had my gender changed on documents, I got people in hospitals calling me &quot;Mr. [Lastname] in front of the whole waiting room, which is downright dangerous. I had to fight a big procedural brawl with the hospital over that. I won, in the end; got the whole branch to change their policy on trans patients. Even saw it show up as a question on the training documents when I renewed my certification the next year. But having to have that fight still left a bad taste in my mouth, and so I don't like to interact with hospitals as a patient more than the minimum necessary to keep on living.<br /> <br /> Also, tip on insurance companies for any trans folks here: most insurance companies are jerks about reimbursing trans-related care, but you can usually con them into paying for HRT by insisting your doctor diagnose the treatment as &quot;endocrine disorder not otherwise specified&quot; instead of anything explicitly trans-related (like &quot;gender dysphoria&quot; or &quot;transgenderism&quot; or whatever). The informed consent clinic I went to to start HRT did it that way as a matter of course, and I've insisted subsequent doctors do it, and that's worked out well for me.<br /> <br /> Speaking of informed consent, that's kind of the answer to the second part of your question. Lots of doctors still require psychiatric approval for hormones, but there's an increasing number of informed consent clinics that basically just require you to affirm that you understand the risks and likely effects and wish to proceed of your own free will. That's how I did it, and I highly recommend it. Psychiatric professionals often have weird ideas about what qualifies you as trans, and some even require RLE (&quot;Real Life Experience,&quot; which means you live as a woman/man for at least a year or two before they'll medically treat you. Hazing for trans people, basically. Imagine if, to get a promotion at your job, you had to act like you already had the promotion while everyone screams at you &quot;Fuck you Becky! You're not actually my boss!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Surgery is a little more closely guarded. Facial surgery usually is informed consent, but genital surgery usually needs at least a full year of both RLE and HRT (which may be concurrent). Also, you usually need two letters from mental health professionals, at least one of which has to have a PhD. Fortunately, unlike HRT, genital surgery usually isn't needed to function in society as your actual gender, so it's easier to wait for. Still a tremendous relief to those who want it when they get it.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I went through that experience recently (SRS, that is). I don't mind answering questions about it for purposes of this thread, if anyone is of a mind to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10290-nine-quiet-lessons","name":"Nine Quiet Lessons","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10290_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T01:20:01-08:00","id":787907,"title":"","content":"Hmm, favorite trans characters? Not really. I have to mirror Baroness Nerak. Again. And of course she's goth as well. WTF's my fetch doing in the US? Anyway, Lesbian/Bi characters do it for me. What I self-identify as is a bi-sexual woman, not transwoman, so... Ah wait! Got one! I quite enjoy the Misfile webcomic.<br /> <br /> Like I already mentioned, over here, for the last 2 years, there has been somewhat of a media offensive regarding the trans topic. Visibility and representation are at a all time high. Articles in all the popular magazines and newspapers, documentaries on tv, one of the characters in the most popular local soap has been outed as trans, etc. Let's see, this week it's 2 articles in the 2 most popular women's magazines, oh, and a transwoman won Holland's Next Topmodel (ok, not really Belgium, but we share media to an extent). It's actually all getting a bit grating. Like we're being hyped or something. Still, it's for the best, I guess.<br /> <br /> Much of the above is thanks to the efforts of the LBGT community. So, in principle, the community is very supportive. In practice, honestly, at the big get-togethers, it's a bit segregated. If you conform to the gender binary, and actually don't look like a trans, it's of course very easy to mix. Anyway, I do conform, am very passable and I actually go 'stealth' as much as I can so I can socialize with others without the baggage. I am rather relieved I can do this, and yes, I am not really proud of this tendency at times. But like I said: I self-identify a bisexual woman, not a transwoman. I'm not ashamed to be a transgender and I can and do talk freely about it, but it feels so good to be treated as just a woman, you know? So, in short: it's still far from ideal if you don't conform to the binary standard, even in the LBGT community, because if you don't, you can stand over there with the trans-clique.<br /> <br /> Now, let's move on to the medical experience. In the university hospital in Gent, they have the 'Gender Team', a multi-disciplinary team, and they can provide everything, from diagnosis, counseling, legal help, HRT, epilation, FFS, SRS, etc. It's an all-in experience, as it were, and a good one at that. They even go as far as to make the things that are not covered by social security, such as FFS, affordable. I simply have no words to express my appreciation for these people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T02:13:39-08:00","id":787930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=787907#post787907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, favorite trans characters? Not really. I have to mirror Baroness Nerak. Again. And of course she's goth as well. WTF's my fetch doing in the US?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, chillin'. Main difference seems to be my place on the sexuality spectrum is different, because my attraction to men is very low (up from nonexistent) while attraction to women is very high, while it sounds like you are closer to middle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Much of the above is thanks to the efforts of the LBGT community. So, in principle, the community is very supportive. In practice, honestly, at the big get-togethers, it's a bit segregated. If you conform to the gender binary, and actually don't look like a trans, it's of course very easy to mix. Anyway, I do conform, am very passable and I actually go 'stealth' as much as I can so I can socialize with others without the baggage. I am rather relieved I can do this, and yes, I am not really proud of this tendency at times. But like I said: I self-identify a bisexual woman, not a transwoman. I'm not ashamed to be a transgender and I can and do talk freely about it, but it feels so good to be treated as just a woman, you know? So, in short: it's still far from ideal if you don't conform to the binary standard, even in the LBGT community, because if you don't, you can stand over there with the trans-clique. </div> </div> </div>Yea, Stealth is not yet an option for me yet but I am hoping. My face is not super masculine, just not super feminine either, but HRT has not changed it really any yet. Not going to deny being a trans woman, and not ashamed of it, but lesbian and woman first. I guess the desire to just be a gal has been so strong, and it is so close. At the same time, I stick with the community...I mean, I started this thread to help with understanding.<br /> <br /> ETA: I also want to thank Nine Quiet Lessons for coming out to support me. She is one of the people that really, really helped me when I was scared and confused, and part of why I am here today at peace with myself. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-17-2015, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T02:47:21-08:00","id":787940,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I'm detracting from a moment of human connection, but I've got an issue that I rarely mention ever to anyone, and maybe it's appropriate here:<br /> <br /> I mostly think of and identity my genitalia as...genitalia. That's as specific as I am to MYSELF in private. My sexual interests mirror the mindset in not generally caring about anatomy as much as situation. I've worried about penis size before, but that was before even driving age, when my peers had assured me that it was a measure of worth as a human being. <br /> With respect to my sexuality, I'm apt to be feminine or masculine, depending on what feels best. I'm not sure if that puts me in a certain category or not. Just saying. I've had girlfriends who acted as the &quot;male&quot; or masculine and more forceful personality in the relationship. I've also had the complete opposite, to the point where my partner decided that they're comfortable calling me everything from dragoste (Romanian ex boyfriend) to Daddy (most of my ex girlfriends) and relied on me for stability and masculine support.<br /> <br /> Throughout all of this, I've maybe eroticized my own junk a half dozen times. Am I just not giving a shit about anatomy? I have no idea. Does MY junk NOT mattering mean something? Orgasms are fine and all, but I don't really associate any eroticism with the anatomical actions or features of my sexual anatomy. <br /> <br /> ...I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 12-17-2015, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T03:55:21-08:00","id":787970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=787930#post787930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, chillin'. Main difference seems to be my place on the sexuality spectrum is different, because my attraction to men is very low (up from nonexistent) while attraction to women is very high, while it sounds like you are closer to middle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I most likely am. But perhaps not? We have not discussed shifts in sexual orientation yet, have we? Let's!<br /> <br /> I really don't know at this point, and must admit to being very confused about this. This is extremely frustrating for me actually. I have not had many sexual encounters with men, but when I had, my gender dysphoria kicked in much harder than with women. It appears I really, really needed to have sex with men as a woman in order to enjoy it, so can I really say I explored that? Also, at the end, to have sex with a woman, I had to imagine I was her, so really, did I want to be with a woman, or just to play with the body I wanted to have?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I know (hope actually) that I'm seriously overthinking this. From the top of my head, there's currently only 1 guy who catches my intrest, and that's been since forever, and for the rest it's almost exclusively women who turn my head. But I have detected an increased reaction. Male pheromones now apparently do something for me, and it unsettles me. But still, even if it's now easier for me to fancy men and enjoy being with them, that wouldn't really change that much, would it? I still prefer women! What's driving me so bonkers and fueling this self-doubt is that I can't engage in anything remotely sexual in nature at this point in my transition. Doing so would shatter the feminine illusion and bring the dysphoria monster out to play. I just can't, Really can't.<br /> <br /> So yeah, that sucks. I have to be patient, but I'm sick of being patient. These issues are among the main reasons why me and my girlfriend have decided to be BFF's for the moment (the other reasons are the change in our dynamics due to me becoming more emotional and 'softer', and the question of just how bisexual she really is). However, we still sleep in the same bed, and whatever limited physical intimacy I can manage, I still do with her. She's patient. She's wonderful.<br /> <br /> But I just can't commit fully until I can sort out this mess. So, patience. Grrrrrrrrr. But really, if I am truly, totally honest, this potential shift in orientation scares me shitless and I can't get it out of my system. What if I like sex with men better? I'd really not want that. Argh. it's all so irrational, because I definitely like looking at and being with women more. Well, except for this one guy. Nooooo.<br /> <br /> And wow, this is longer than I wanted, and reads a bit like how disjointed, over-obsessed and circular my thinking on the subject now is. You hit a nerve there, Baroness. This, for me, hands down, the hardest part of the transition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=787930#post787930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, Stealth is not yet an option for me yet but I am hoping. My face is not super masculine, just not super feminine either, but HRT has not changed it really any yet. Not going to deny being a trans woman, and not ashamed of it, but lesbian and woman first. I guess the desire to just be a gal has been so strong, and it is so close.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hormones will make indeed your face a bit softer and give your skin that feminine glow. That, and the right attitude will go a long way. <br /> <br /> Yes, we're close :-) But as you can read in my rant above, the closer you get, the more unbearable the wait ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T04:29:32-08:00","id":787984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=787940#post787940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if I'm detracting from a moment of human connection, but I've got an issue that I rarely mention ever to anyone, and maybe it's appropriate here:<br /> <br /> I mostly think of and identity my genitalia as...genitalia. That's as specific as I am to MYSELF in private. My sexual interests mirror the mindset in not generally caring about anatomy as much as situation. I've worried about penis size before, but that was before even driving age, when my peers had assured me that it was a measure of worth as a human being.<br /> With respect to my sexuality, I'm apt to be feminine or masculine, depending on what feels best. I'm not sure if that puts me in a certain category or not. Just saying. I've had girlfriends who acted as the &quot;male&quot; or masculine and more forceful personality in the relationship. I've also had the complete opposite, to the point where my partner decided that they're comfortable calling me everything from dragoste (Romanian ex boyfriend) to Daddy (most of my ex girlfriends) and relied on me for stability and masculine support.<br /> <br /> Throughout all of this, I've maybe eroticized my own junk a half dozen times. Am I just not giving a shit about anatomy? I have no idea. Does MY junk NOT mattering mean something? Orgasms are fine and all, but I don't really associate any eroticism with the anatomical actions or features of my sexual anatomy.<br /> <br /> ...I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not distracting at all :-)<br /> <br /> And yes, I think your junk not mattering means something. More important in my opinion is your statement that you can shift from a feminine to a masculine mindset depending on situation and partner. This definitely sounds like you're gender-fluid and might explain your issues, or better perhaps, your total lack of issues with your genitalia.<br /> <br /> I'm about as far away from gender-fluid as you can get, but it resonates with what I've heard from gender-fluid guys and gals, so I believe that direction is worth exploring.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T06:39:26-08:00","id":788038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=787940#post787940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if I'm detracting from a moment of human connection, but I've got an issue that I rarely mention ever to anyone, and maybe it's appropriate here:<br /> <br /> I mostly think of and identity my genitalia as...genitalia. That's as specific as I am to MYSELF in private. My sexual interests mirror the mindset in not generally caring about anatomy as much as situation. I've worried about penis size before, but that was before even driving age, when my peers had assured me that it was a measure of worth as a human being. <br /> With respect to my sexuality, I'm apt to be feminine or masculine, depending on what feels best. I'm not sure if that puts me in a certain category or not. Just saying. I've had girlfriends who acted as the &amp;quot;male&amp;quot; or masculine and more forceful personality in the relationship. I've also had the complete opposite, to the point where my partner decided that they're comfortable calling me everything from dragoste (Romanian ex boyfriend) to Daddy (most of my ex girlfriends) and relied on me for stability and masculine support.<br /> <br /> Throughout all of this, I've maybe eroticized my own junk a half dozen times. Am I just not giving a shit about anatomy? I have no idea. Does MY junk NOT mattering mean something? Orgasms are fine and all, but I don't really associate any eroticism with the anatomical actions or features of my sexual anatomy. <br /> <br /> ...I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the camp that believes what you personally feel is more important than if you match a description. I mean, being able to shift between masculine and feminine mindsets certainly sounds like some kind of gender fluidity to me, but I don't think what it sounds like to me matters as much as what it feels like to you. If anything, it might be a sign to look more into the different groups that fall under the Trans umbrella and see if any of them resonate with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T06:46:20-08:00","id":788046,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit late to the game, and it's been rough lately, but I'd like to give my own thoughts if that's ok?<br /> <br /> I realized I was trans probably around 5-7... but due to home life and other stuff suppressed it a lot, to the point that I didn't think of myself that way till I was 21. North Dakota and my father are not exactly kind towards those who are different, and in my home town I already had problems because it was very small, they didn't like &quot;outsiders&quot; (true story, over 80% of my grade school class were related to the rest, as cousins generally), so... I consider myself a lesbian woman.<br /> <br /> I'm going to mostly mirror Baroness here that I identify/enjoy lesbian and bi characters more than trans, BUT... I think that's in part due to sometimes a real problem with the presentation of them. I'll second Misfile though.<br /> <br /> On treatment by the umbrella groups... I've had some pretty awful experiences with gay men. And considering I have a bit of fear towards white men for past history, though I try and keep it reasonable, and living in a very white state... I've not taken that sort of thing well. I am not holding a grudge or anything, but it makes me hesitant. I feel like there's a real set of problems not just for trans, but younger people and those who aren't white (especially if you mix these). Look at pride events and how much they can cost, or look at the recent history of Christopher Street Pier in New York City. I don't think it's a universal thing, but there are those groups who through ignorance or malice can cause harm (more often ignorance, but malice can be real, such as in the case of some TERFs).<br /> <br /> To me, I find sex kinda not nearly as meaningful a term as gender, and frankly what I'd say has no criteria that makes sense. I studied a lot of biotechnology which has a lot of genetics and such, and generally take a strong interest in biology (and had to take as much biochemistry as any pre-med or pharmacy student at the uni), so I feel I know a bit about what I'm talking about. Genetics has so many cases where people don't fit into the neat boxes of male or female, so it doesn't work. You can't look just at physical structure externally or even really internally, because there are many many things that show it doesn't work (as a few, intersex, issues where someone who is assigned a female gender develops male genitalia in puberty, etc...). Hormones are so wildly variable as to not work. In the end, gender is the only one that can be identified reasonably well, and that's because the person can say (publically or just to their own self) who they feel they are.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this is helpful at all and hope no one minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T10:19:30-08:00","id":788186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=787930#post787930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ETA: I also want to thank Nine Quiet Lessons for coming out to support me. She is one of the people that really, really helped me when I was scared and confused, and part of why I am here today at peace with myself. Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you; that's very sweet and it made me smile this morning. It was my pleasure to be part of your story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throughout all of this, I've maybe eroticized my own junk a half dozen times. Am I just not giving a shit about anatomy? I have no idea. Does MY junk NOT mattering mean something? Orgasms are fine and all, but I don't really associate any eroticism with the anatomical actions or features of my sexual anatomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that <i>most </i>people probably don't eroticize their own junk. If it's all in working order, it's just sort of there, and you probably don't think about it too much except when something is <i>not </i>working properly.<br /> <br /> Also, to add to that: expressing yourself in a more masculine or feminine manner doesn't have to have implications for your identity. We're all somewhere on a spectrum between completely &quot;male&quot; and completely &quot;female,&quot; and male and female anyway are imprecise social constructs that only hint at the underlying reality, which is that what we recognize as gender is a complex set of loosely-linked traits that each exist on separate spectra. There was a recent (often-misquoted) paper [<a href=\"http://www.pnas.org/content/112/50/15468.abstract]\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.pnas.org/content/112/50/15468.abstract]</a> on brain sex indicating that most people have brains that are a mosaic of &quot;male&quot; and &quot;female&quot; traits. Likewise with other gendered traits.<br /> <br /> It's the same with gender expression; we all have personality traits that are stereotypically male and female, especially when those categories are so broadly construed as to define bravery as &quot;masculine&quot; and empathy as &quot;feminine.&quot; Yet, we (almost) all can be brave, and we (almost) all can empathize with others. Being able to switch modes of expression makes you flexible, but it doesn't make you (for example) &quot;not a man.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, if on the other hand, something about being a man felt &quot;off&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; to you, then there might be an issue with your identity. But I don't get the sense that that's the case, from what you've written.<br /> <br /> It reminds me of a bit from Susan Stryker's essay [<a href=\"https://tidsskrift.dk/index.php/KKF/article/view/44377/84150]\" target=\"_blank\">https://tidsskrift.dk/index.php/KKF/...w/44377/84150]</a>. We're obliged to construct our identities around ideas of an essentialist masculinity/femininity divide, but those ideas are themselves constructs. Which, I think (if you'll let me drift even more off topic) is where a lot of the fear towards transgender people comes from, because if you think too long about the implications of trans-ness, you're at risk of (as Stryker says) discovering the &quot;seams and sutures in yourself.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10290-nine-quiet-lessons","name":"Nine Quiet Lessons","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10290_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T10:22:45-08:00","id":788190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=788046#post788046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, I find sex kinda not nearly as meaningful a term as gender, and frankly what I'd say has no criteria that makes sense. I studied a lot of biotechnology which has a lot of genetics and such, and generally take a strong interest in biology (and had to take as much biochemistry as any pre-med or pharmacy student at the uni), so I feel I know a bit about what I'm talking about. Genetics has so many cases where people don't fit into the neat boxes of male or female, so it doesn't work. You can't look just at physical structure externally or even really internally, because there are many many things that show it doesn't work (as a few, intersex, issues where someone who is assigned a female gender develops male genitalia in puberty, etc...). Hormones are so wildly variable as to not work. In the end, gender is the only one that can be identified reasonably well, and that's because the person can say (publically or just to their own self) who they feel they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Total agreement! Also, what you wrote mirrors the recent Nature article (&quot;Sex Redefined&quot; [<a href=\"http://www.nature.com/news/sex-redefined-1.16943]\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nature.com/news/sex-redefined-1.16943]</a>) that comes to much the same conclusion, which is pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Also, always nice to see another trans biologist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10290-nine-quiet-lessons","name":"Nine Quiet Lessons","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10290_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T11:39:36-08:00","id":788242,"title":"","content":"Angwe: I sympathize, a lot of that (attraction to women vs. men and how it dovetails into my identity) is how I felt before getting on hormones. I am not, at this point, worried about losing much of any interest in women. My interest in women remains pretty strong. My sex drive is (slightly) lower, but I think hormones are only going to affect my orientation so much. Going from personal experience to what I have been told, I have been told if your desire for women is not exclusively projection but a strong interest in ourselves as women, you will continue to desire us. If your interests were pretty much the woman as surrogate you, you may find yourself straighter as you lose any need for a surrogate. For me, I desire women because I desire women; I just greatly prefer interacting with them as a woman. Also, good god that last part sounded objectifying. Sorry I can't think of how to phrase it better &gt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> I suspect being less interested in men is part of why I have less (but not no) genital dysphoria. Which is good; affording surgery is a huge pipe dream, I am unsure if I ever would be able to. All things being equal I would like to, but I can't see at this point how it could possibly happen.<br /> <br /> AF: This is the thread for that kind of thing. I want to have non-trans people feel like they can ask and get clarification without being judged, or yelled at, or insulted, which is too rare. I also want people with any amount of genderqueer to them to be able to ask questions and learn about themselves without being judged, yelled at, or insulted. So you are good.<br /> <br /> Haren: It's all good, thanks for posting. As I told AF, this is a place for it. I am sorry you have had a rough time.<br /> <br /> 9QL: I don't have much to add except I agree with everything you said. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T12:36:33-08:00","id":788274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=788242#post788242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also want people with any amount of genderqueer to them to be able to ask questions and learn about themselves without being judged, yelled at, or insulted. So you are good.</div> </div> </div> </div>This thread has been really helpful for me. I feel like I should share my very messy story. I've typed up variations of this for this thread over the past few days, but never posted it. A bit because it may be off topic. Mostly out of fear, because while I don't hide my gender on this forum, I try not to draw attention to it.<br /> <br /> And out of shame, because I have done things I regret.<br /> <br /> I had a lot of difficulty going though puberty. It took me a while to realize this was less because I wanted boy parts, but because my family's fear of me becoming a victim of sexual violence - taken advantage of- had a negative impact on how I viewed both genders. Whenever I hung out with my geeky male friends, I always got the &quot;talk&quot; to be careful and to be aware when they would try to do something inappropriate to me. (They never did.) My family was very much against me moving away for college, because girls shouldn't move away for college. They wanted me to go to the same local fourth tier university my mother did (Thankfully my mother supported me going to the college I wanted). Later, when I kicked my college boyfriend out and decided to live alone, they worried because it was dangerous for a young lady to live alone. I brought up joining the Peace Corps, and got stories about how dangerous it was to be woman overseas.<br /> <br /> I did not want to grow up, because growing up meant that fifty percent of the population would cease to see me as an individual, but rather something to fuck. I hated that. I hated being a woman because it was barrier against doing what I wanted with my life. Because of this, I had negative views of feminine woman. How stupid do you have to be to want to be treated as a thing, instead of a thinking individual? The bar for my expectations of men was set so low, that I made a lot of poor choices for who to be in a relationship with.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm 33. I realize that my earlier views on gender were colored by my upbringing. I still have a negative reaction when someone brings up little girls being princesses. Once I expressed an interest in websites that have sciencey clothing for girls, someone else expressed a need for pink Dora the Explorer clothing items for boys. I had to stay quiet, because my first reaction was &quot;WHY! Why would you do that to your son!?!&quot; Not rational, very awful. I'm ashamed to post these thoughts in a Trans-Gender thread, because I feel like I've been part of the problem sometimes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The majority of my RP characters start out in my head as male. I switch them for real life play, but on forums, I keep them male. When I was planning on my Exalted Quest Game, I briefly considered making the main character female. We already had a male quest character on the Exalted forum and I have often said that there was a general need for more female characters in stories. I had such a negative reaction to writing about a female child going though puberty, I kept the character male. I couldn't bear going though female puberty again. I knew I couldn't deal with someone spouting the same &quot;Girls should be Careful&quot; crap I got as a teenager. I did not want my character to be limited by their gender, not for a first writing project. Now I know that the odds of that happening on this forum are zero, but I did have a nasty flame war with one of the more conservative members about sex. The fear was not easily extinguished.<br /> <br /> Yet, when I make an MMORPG character, they are female. As a child, I identified with gender neutral characters like Data or Odo. As an adult, I still identify with them (see Gir Avatar) but also with female characters. The Agender Identity intrigues me, but the label never seemed to fit me right. I don't care if you call me sir/ma'am, he/she, but if you ask, I'll tell you I'm female. I think Agender expression fits me better and I am very happy to discover that was a thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T12:59:27-08:00","id":788286,"title":"","content":"Wonderandawe: It's no problem. This is as I say the place for it. I can see how your views of femininity would make it repulsive for you. It's...obviously a different view than I have. I don't view myself as becoming an object at all. But looking at modern culture I CAN see why you would feel that way. We are treated as objects a lot. For me it's balancing femininity with strength of a sort. And it's part of why women's spaces are so important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T13:09:14-08:00","id":788294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=788286#post788286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonderandawe: It's no problem. This is as I say the place for it. I can see how your views of femininity would make it repulsive for you. It's...obviously a different view than I have. I don't view myself as becoming an object at all. But looking at modern culture I CAN see why you would feel that way. We are treated as objects a lot. For me it's balancing femininity with strength of a sort. And it's part of why women's spaces are so important.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. I realize this view of &quot;expressing femininity is asking to be treated as an object&quot; is unhealthy. I'd like to think of myself as an open-minded person but then someone will say something and my first reaction always shocks me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Safe places are good for all genders. I am a member of a knitting guild, so that is a good place to meet with woman and talk about making girly accessories. I'm still at the point where I like making them more than wearing them, but baby steps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you for your support. I feel a lot better expressing this. It's been on my mind for years, but it is something that is easier to write out than say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T16:15:11-08:00","id":788380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=788274#post788274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a lot of difficulty going though puberty. It took me a while to realize this was less because I wanted boy parts, but because my family's fear of me becoming a victim of sexual violence - taken advantage of- had a negative impact on how I viewed both genders. Whenever I hung out with my geeky male friends, I always got the &quot;talk&quot; to be careful and to be aware when they would try to do something inappropriate to me. (They never did.) My family was very much against me moving away for college, because girls shouldn't move away for college. They wanted me to go to the same local fourth tier university my mother did (Thankfully my mother supported me going to the college I wanted). Later, when I kicked my college boyfriend out and decided to live alone, they worried because it was dangerous for a young lady to live alone. I brought up joining the Peace Corps, and got stories about how dangerous it was to be woman overseas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your experience sounds remarkably similar to things my girlfriend has told me about her life, growing up. Actually, a lot of AFAB folks have said similar things to me, about how they were always being told to be afraid.<br /> <br /> I didn't get that, growing up, though I sort of came to it later in life; I get a lot of cautionary advice from my mom, now. I'm still more willing to, say, walk alone on dark streets than most of my cis women cohorts, though. Truth be told, I tend to feel a little safer when it's dark and isolated than when it's crowded and full of people; I've always got the fear that if I get de-stealthed as trans in public, groups of people could turn uglier than any single person.<br /> <br /> I think it colors my perception, too, that the one time I <i>did</i> get assaulted at night, it was pre-transition and I was presenting fairly male-ish. So I never felt like the male camouflage was that protective for me; maybe I was doing it wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not want to grow up, because growing up meant that fifty percent of the population would cease to see me as an individual, but rather something to fuck. I hated that. I hated being a woman because it was barrier against doing what I wanted with my life. Because of this, I had negative views of feminine woman. How stupid do you have to be to want to be treated as a thing, instead of a thinking individual?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it helps explain or not, but this is how I came to have the relationship I have with femininity:<br /> <br /> I didn't go into transition expecting to particularly feminine. When I was doing the male presentation thing, it was pretty rare for me to wear anything other than black or blue jeans and a solid-color t-shirt (usually black). I even had people joke to me that they thought my closet must have rows of identical jeans and black t-shirts. So when I thought of myself as a woman, I imagined I would carry forward pretty much the same presentation, except the clothes would be cut for a woman's figure and I'd have breasts.<br /> <br /> But part of transition was that I got to re-invent myself and my personal style, so I experimented a little and found that I did enjoy doing the whole high-femme thing. Makeup, fancy shoes, dresses, and all that. I don't indulge in that most days, since being constantly dressed to the nines doesn't exactly help one blend in. But when a special occasion presents itself, I do enjoy it. I actually feel <i>more </i>powerful and in charge on those occasions. Maybe because, for so long, it wasn't <i>required </i>of me, but rather <i>forbidden</i>.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the point is that it's something I do for myself, not for anyone else, except inasmuch as I feel like dressing nice is a way of showing respect for other people. I know not everyone feels that way (I had an argument with my girlfriend once, when I showed up for a date in a carefully-chosen outfit, and when I got there she was in a bathrobe). So I don't see it as advertising myself as a sexual ware to be consumed, or as marking me as less intelligent, but rather as a way of taking control of my appearance and of communicating myself to other people.<br /> <br /> I want to be clear, I'm not criticizing you or disagreeing with your experience; I'm really glad you shared your own story, and it gave me some stuff to think about when I reflected it through my own experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10290-nine-quiet-lessons","name":"Nine Quiet Lessons","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10290_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T16:55:09-08:00","id":788403,"title":"","content":"Yea I feel best when I am in lacy black stuff with as gothic make-up as I can get my hands on on. I don't feel especially like a commodity, though I want to be pleasing* for women who see me.<br /> <br /> *I realize many/most women are not into women at all. I also realize fewer are than are into men. I am, obviously, not doing this for sex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-17-2015, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T16:59:43-08:00","id":788404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nine Quiet Lessons</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=788380#post788380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But part of transition was that I got to re-invent myself and my personal style, so I experimented a little and found that I did enjoy doing the whole high-femme thing. Makeup, fancy shoes, dresses, and all that. I don't indulge in that most days, since being constantly dressed to the nines doesn't exactly help one blend in. But when a special occasion presents itself, I do enjoy it. I actually feel <i>more </i>powerful and in charge on those occasions. Maybe because, for so long, it wasn't <i>required </i>of me, but rather <i>forbidden</i>.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the point is that it's something I do for myself, not for anyone else, except inasmuch as I feel like dressing nice is a way of showing respect for other people. I know not everyone feels that way (I had an argument with my girlfriend once, when I showed up for a date in a carefully-chosen outfit, and when I got there she was in a bathrobe). So I don't see it as advertising myself as a sexual ware to be consumed, or as marking me as less intelligent, but rather as a way of taking control of my appearance and of communicating myself to other people.<br /> <br /> I want to be clear, I'm not criticizing you or disagreeing with your experience; I'm really glad you shared your own story, and it gave me some stuff to think about when I reflected it through my own experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, I love drag queen shows. I love the freedom to tell society to fuck off and act and dress how you want.<br /> <br /> I do own makeup and dresses now. I see it more as a freedom thing. I wear what I want no matter what gender it protrays. I love eyeshadow in its various bright colors, though I rarely wear it. <br /> <br /> I want to pick up some dapper clothing, but I don't like to buy clothes online and that seems to be my only option for clothes that fix my figure.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/ee/72/52/ee72528ba41960400440ac513b540ee6.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-17-2015, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T17:52:22-08:00","id":788423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=788403#post788403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea I feel best when I am in lacy black stuff with as gothic make-up as I can get my hands on on. I don't feel especially like a commodity, though I want to be pleasing* for women who see me.<br /> <br /> *I realize many/most women are not into women at all. I also realize fewer are than are into men. I am, obviously, not doing this for sex.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I understand you right, (and I might be totally wrong) the woman you want to please the most is... yourself. I'm not saying you don't want to look nice for others, but in the end, I think most people want to feel comfortable with how they look. Like people I've known who got plastic surgery said &quot;This isn't for other people... this is FOR ME.&quot; Clothes are less of a permanent thing, but it's along the same spectrum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T19:57:41-08:00","id":788487,"title":"","content":"Yea I dress up for myself first. other ladies second. I am not exactly bugged by any guys who enjoy my appearance either, of course. Anything more long term would be the same way, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T01:21:13-08:00","id":788597,"title":"","content":"BN: Thank you for your empathy. With me there's indeed a fair amount of projection going on during sex. But my interest in women definitely goes a whole lot deeper than that. So I'll think it'll be fine, even if my orientation shifts more towards the middle. That'll hardly be the end of the world. If this, and the question whether I prefer the girl who I share my bed with to be my best friend (with benefits) or my girlfriend, I have absolutely nothing to complain about. Compared to other issues, these are truly petty, little first world problems.<br /> <br /> Such as Haren's story (all my sympathies!) or not being able to afford SRS. I am so very sorry to hear that. Angry too! SRS is for the greatest part covered by our social security, so it only costs 3.5K \u20ac here. Health &amp; mental care should always be accessible to those who need it. <br /> <br /> Wonderandawe: thank you for sharing your experiences. For what it's worth, from my time, ahem, 'undercover' on the other side of the gender-border, the true creeps are a minority. Still way too many, though.<br /> <br /> I also enjoy 'dolling up', but get to indulge it way too rarely. Me and the gf have horses, you see, so on a daily basis sensible, practical clothing is definitely the way to go. But when I do, it's for my own enjoyment and the way it makes me feel empowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T01:47:35-08:00","id":788607,"title":"","content":"That makes sense.<br /> <br /> Well I am optimistic. LGBT rights have been moving with unprecedented speed, and I do have hormones covered. I can only hope coverage gets more common. We have been moving in the correct direction. The US remains a bit behind, but I am hopeful.<br /> <br /> Besides, my gaming group is here, and finally well trained. ^_^<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T06:44:18-08:00","id":788719,"title":"","content":"Well, I hope things improve soon! Honestly, still progress to be made here as well. Laser epilation and FFS are not covered by social security. But at least for the FFS the university hospital is pushing the research that this is just as important as the SRS. Also, they offer the FFS at base cost because, I'll quote the surgeon: &quot;It's very vital for your process and anyway, we're here to help people and not to get rich from our patients misery.&quot;. I was speechless and could only manage to stammer a weak &quot;thank you&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T16:28:57-08:00","id":791148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=787588#post787588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What were your experiences, if any, dealing with nurses, doctors, insurance companies? Do they still require a psychiatrist approval before any hormone therapy or surgery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanted to cover this one specifically from a UK POV:<br /> <br /> Currently, trans healthcare treatment is <i>in theory</i> governed by the Interim Guidelines, in England. (Scotland, NI and I believe Wales have their own procedures; in generally it's better to be trans in Scotland and worse in NI wrt the NHS). You can search for them easily enough; in general they're a huge improvement, but things are still... not great.<br /> <br /> Your GP should refer you to a GIC, who will then interview you, then can do things like prescribe HRT or refer you for other services like facial hair removal. Some time after that you can start being considered for surgeries (generally mastectomies - top surgery - are treated less restrictively than genital reconstruction, because they're easier (and with my cynical hat on more palatable to cis people)). Your GP will monitor your bloodwork and general health, and the GIC will review your bloods and do anything your GP is not equipped for. Unless your GP or GIC wants to, because they feel your mental health is not stable enough for whatever, the mental health trust is not involved, and 'real life experience' requirements (ugh) have been removed for everything, except possibly SRS, I forget.<br /> <br /> The two big problems in the UK right now are time and discrimination. Both GPs and specialists may well have an attitude ranging from reticent to paternalistic to outright contempt for trans patients, slowing you down or making you start again in some other clinic. (<i>oh boy</i> are there specialists with contempt for their patients.) The restrictive way everything is set up means that you might wait anywhere from six months to <i>three years</i> (or more) for your first referral, then spread three hours of consultation over a further <i>six to nine months</i> before you're provided with any actual care. If you're non-binary or otherwise don't conform to your specialists' ideas of how you should do your gender, you might be faced with a frustrating fight to make them believe that you're 'serious'.<br /> <br /> Of course this is all in the NHS. According to Mr. Cameron if we'd just let the private sector take over you'd be treated with unicorn farts the day you walked in the door, but idk about that myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T03:32:25-08:00","id":792082,"title":"","content":"I dunno, crabbadon, I hear there's a high success rate of cures with unicorn farts. 9 out of 10 snake oil salesmen agree!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T04:39:48-08:00","id":818333,"title":"","content":"I meant to ask before but slipped my mind. There was mention of something called &quot;chaser mentallity&quot; and how that was undesirable. Can you explain what does this mean and what entails?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T05:17:40-08:00","id":818347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818333#post818333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant to ask before but slipped my mind. There was mention of something called &quot;chaser mentallity&quot; and how that was undesirable. Can you explain what does this mean and what entails?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The best way I can think to describe this is fetishization of trans people. Those who &quot;chase&quot; trans people not for who they are but because they're trans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:19:46-08:00","id":818371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818347#post818347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way I can think to describe this is fetishization of trans people. Those who &quot;chase&quot; trans people not for who they are but because they're trans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I fail to see how this is any different from people looking for a specific body type, hair color or even skin color. Everybody has preferences. Some people would probably prefer a cis or trans person over the other, some probably wouldn't care at all. What's the difference with, say, a woman looking for a tall man?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:22:37-08:00","id":818375,"title":"","content":"It reduces someone down to a single aspect of their body, rather than treating them as a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:46:02-08:00","id":818388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818371#post818371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I fail to see how this is any different from people looking for a specific body type, hair color or even skin color. Everybody has preferences. Some people would probably prefer a cis or trans person over the other, some probably wouldn't care at all. What's the difference with, say, a woman looking for a tall man?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of those things can also be fetishization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:19:12-08:00","id":818402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818388#post818388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of those things can also be fetishization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh they most certainly can, I just fail to see what's wrong with <i>preferences</i>. Fetishization of a person can quickly fall into the person-as-an-object territory and that's bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It reduces someone down to a single aspect of their body, rather than treating them as a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it means that on the superficial level (say you're scrolling Tinder) you'll be looking for what you prefer, usually physically. If your ideal man is blond, tall, athletic, caucasian and cis, then all of those factors will affect your vision of the guys you'll see. If someone fulfills all categories except the Cis part, you might be interested in learning more about him, same goes if he's ginger or smaller. But a short fat ginger coloured trans guy would not be to your liking because he fulfills basically none of your ideals, as superficial as they might be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:21:58-08:00","id":818404,"title":"","content":"Chiming in for a second, because this is an awesome thread.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818371#post818371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I fail to see how this is any different from people looking for a specific body type, hair color or even skin color. Everybody has preferences. Some people would probably prefer a cis or trans person over the other, some probably wouldn't care at all. What's the difference with, say, a woman looking for a tall man?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point. But it's like the difference between liking redheads and going out of your way to hit and try to &quot;score&quot; with every redhead you see, just because of that detail.<br /> <br /> One is perfectly fine, the other... less so.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:31:14-08:00","id":818410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818402#post818402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh they most certainly can, I just fail to see what's wrong with <i>preferences</i>. Fetishization of a person can quickly fall into the person-as-an-object territory and that's bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall anyone here saying there was anything wrong with preferences. Thorbes asked what was meant by &quot;chaser mentality&quot;, and the answer is that chasers are people who fetishize trans people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818234-non-charming-uses-of-majesty?p=818393#post818393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it means that on the superficial level (say you're scrolling Tinder) you'll be looking for what you prefer, usually physically. If your ideal man is blond, tall, athletic, caucasian and cis, then all of those factors will affect your vision of the guys you'll see. If someone fulfills all categories except the Cis part, you might be interested in learning more about him, same goes if he's ginger or smaller. But a short fat ginger coloured trans guy would not be to your liking because he fulfills basically none of your ideals, as superficial as they might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. The thing about having a &quot;preference for trans people&quot; though is that it is often focused on their genitals being different from those of cis people of the same gender. That's an inherently transphobic mentality, because you're basing your attraction on how they're &quot;different from other women&quot;. Being turned on because I'm a woman with a penis is not any better than being grossed out because I'm a woman with a penis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T08:03:33-08:00","id":818429,"title":"","content":"I also think there's a sort of exoticism going on there as well. Which is troubling in different ways without focusing on genitals. There's probably a few focuses for chasers, but they aren't kind towards trans people in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:16:22-08:00","id":818593,"title":"","content":"I really have no experience with chasers, so not much to add.<br /> <br /> There is a line. Some people prefer trans women. Some people prefer cis women. For some people, of both preferences, genitalia is a factor. For others, it isn't. I have a friend who is Korean. She is quick to say some of those interested in her want an &quot;oriental beauty&quot; and fetishize her. Some don't. She has dated guys who prefer Asian women, but don't seem to have any of her red flags (wanting her to act submissively, wanting her to dress as a schoolgirl or in stereotypical Asian clothes, wanting to marry oddly quickly for dating a guy, etc)<br /> <br /> So I imagine something like that.<br /> <br /> There is the added thing that particular types of tightly Closeted guys can be INCREDIBLY creepy. I don't mean guys who are not out, I mean guys like a lot of the anti-gay activists who sleep with men. They tend to have resentment toward their partner, and a number of them like Trans women because we don't trigger some of their guilt issues. As if their bizarre behavior was not enough, one can end up hurt or dead from being around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:39:40-08:00","id":818608,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, I have little experience with chasers, since I've lived in what would be not major metropolitan areas with a fair number of trans people. But I've had a number of friends elsewhere who have had those sorts of run-ins. What they always say is it NEVER ends with anything less than some self-hate... though this was with chasers who were capable enough to hide their nature long enough for a relationship to start. Those I've met was only online for the very reasons Baroness Nerak mention.<br /> <br /> It's a real problem, and it comes down to treating the trans person as more an object of lust than a person with valid feelings. It's dehumanizing. It's painful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:06:26-08:00","id":818622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818410#post818410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. The thing about having a &quot;preference for trans people&quot; though is that it is often focused on their genitals being different from those of cis people of the same gender. That's an inherently transphobic mentality, because you're basing your attraction on how they're &quot;different from other women&quot;. Being turned on because I'm a woman with a penis is not any better than being grossed out because I'm a woman with a penis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that an inherently transphobic mentality? People can have preferences for hair colour, hobbies, eye colour, lip form? Why not genitals? How is genitals any special from other traits of human body, on which someone can base his preference?<br /> <br /> Also.. I don't know what &quot;chasers&quot; are, which have been mentioned here, and my question assumes we're talking normal people and not abusive creeps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:16:55-08:00","id":818629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818622#post818622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is that an inherently transphobic mentality? People can have preferences for hair colour, hobbies, eye colour, lip form? Why not genitals? How is genitals any special from other traits of human body, on which someone can base his preference?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the attraction to a particular set of genitals that's the problem, it's the attraction to a particular set of genitals <i>on a person of a particular gender</i>. If you like dicks, that's one thing. If you like women who have dicks because that's not what cis women have, you're focused on how we're different from cis women, and that's what's transphobic about it. I don't want to be the object of attraction because I'm a dickgirl and that's so exotic and hot. I want to be a woman that you are attracted to or not according to your tastes, just like any other woman would be.<br /> <br /> (Note, I'm using the general form of you, not talking about anyone specifically).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818622#post818622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also.. I don't know what &quot;chasers&quot; are, which have been mentioned here, and my question assumes we're talking normal people and not abusive creeps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chasers are people who fetishize trans people, which is a creepy and abusive thing to do. If you're talking about normal people who aren't abusive creeps, you're not talking about the same people I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:36:16-08:00","id":818642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818629#post818629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the attraction to a particular set of genitals that's the problem, it's the attraction to a particular set of genitals <i>on a person of a particular gender</i>. If you like dicks, that's one thing. If you like women who have dicks because that's not what cis women have, you're focused on how we're different from cis women, and that's what's transphobic about it. I don't want to be the object of attraction because I'm a dickgirl and that's so exotic and hot. I want to be a woman that you are attracted to or not according to your tastes, just like any other woman would be.<br /> <br /> (Note, I'm using the general form of you, not talking about anyone specifically).<br /> <br /> <br /> Chasers are people who fetishize trans people, which is a creepy and abusive thing to do. If you're talking about normal people who aren't abusive creeps, you're not talking about the same people I am.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok but... say I don't like dicks but I'm interested in someone and they happen to be a transwoman is it transphobic to gently explain the situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:50:39-08:00","id":818654,"title":"","content":"For me personally, I don't really care which set of genitals my partner prefers, so long as mine are relevant to their interests. In a long term situation, it is a bigger factor. <br /> <br /> But it is like...I like black hair and I like blonde hair. I have never dated or slept with anyone <i>because</i> they had black or blonde hair. That was a plus on the list, but most of my partners have had brown. It's not a fetish, It's never the reason.<br /> <br /> Again, though, I've not had the bad experiences some people have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:56:21-08:00","id":818657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818642#post818642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok but... say I don't like dicks but I'm interested in someone and they happen to be a transwoman is it transphobic to gently explain the situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's about the same as any physical feature you would consider a deal breaker on its own. It doesn't make you a bad person or anything, but you might want to take a look at why this one physical feature carries so much weight for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:00:31-08:00","id":818662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818642#post818642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok but... say I don't like dicks but I'm interested in someone and they happen to be a transwoman is it transphobic to gently explain the situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, only speaking for myself here:<br /> <br /> I'd say no. It's how you do it. For me, if someone I was interested in didn't like penises, and wanted to know if I had one before things got too far, I would not think less of that person. There was a point in time I felt the same way, truth be told, though that is no longer the case. Now (outside, obviously, questions like this, this is absolutely the place. whole point of the thread) I would not make a point of advertising it, it just makes people feel bad. But you have a right to your preferences, and someone not interested in transwomen with...legacy equipment...but still regards us as women is fine.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.