llow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, only speaking for myself here:<br /> <br /> I'd say no. It's how you do it. For me, if someone I was interested in didn't like penises, and wanted to know if I had one before things got too far, I would not think less of that person. There was a point in time I felt the same way, truth be told, though that is no longer the case. Now (outside, obviously, questions like this, this is absolutely the place. whole point of the thread) I would not make a point of advertising it, it just makes people feel bad. But you have a right to your preferences, and someone not interested in transwomen with...legacy equipment...but still regards us as women is fine.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh certainly. I'm not talking about &quot;What the ****!? You're a <b>dude!?&quot; </b>reaction because that's just being a douchebag. I was simply trying to understand that we were on the same page as far as genitalia preferences go. Not that these preferences apply to me, but knowing what's right and wrong is usually a good thing even if you never intended to do the wrong thing.<br /> <br /> Speaking about sexual activities, if you don't mind (and you totally have the right to tell me it's none of my business), but how does it go with first-time sexual partners? Is it something you usually disclose beforehand? Do you simply get there and act perfectly natural? I'm asking because I suppose it might act as a surprise for some people if they're in the heat of the moment and you have legacy equipment, to borrow your terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:19:49-08:00","id":818676,"title":"","content":"I have not had any new partners since transitioning. When/if it happens, they will know before any fluids of any sort are exchanged. When/if I get SRS, that part will no longer be the case by default, but I will probably disclose just cuz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:49:30-08:00","id":818702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818672#post818672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh certainly. I'm not talking about &amp;quot;What the ****!? You're a <b>dude!?&amp;quot; </b>reaction because that's just being a douchebag. I was simply trying to understand that we were on the same page as far as genitalia preferences go. Not that these preferences apply to me, but knowing what's right and wrong is usually a good thing even if you never intended to do the wrong thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable. Different trans people will have different takes on what they consider acceptable. It sounds like Nerak is a bit more on the understanding side than I am, but for the most part I agree with her sentiment. People are allowed to have preferences, just be respectful about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818672#post818672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking about sexual activities, if you don't mind (and you totally have the right to tell me it's none of my business), but how does it go with first-time sexual partners? Is it something you usually disclose beforehand? Do you simply get there and act perfectly natural? I'm asking because I suppose it might act as a surprise for some people if they're in the heat of the moment and you have legacy equipment, to borrow your terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the same boat as Nerak on this one. I've been with my current partner since before I had fully come to terms with being trans, and we are for all intents and purposes monogamous, so this is fortunately not something I've had to deal with. They're also pan, so it wasn't a problem for them at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:55:27-08:00","id":818803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818702#post818702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in the same boat as Nerak on this one. I've been with my current partner since before I had fully come to terms with being trans, and we are for all intents and purposes monogamous, so this is fortunately not something I've had to deal with. They're also pan, so it wasn't a problem for them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I am married and we have mischief options, as long as we follow some rules, so I don't foresee any other long term partners (unless tragedy happens or we both fall in love with the same person) but short term could come up. My wife is Bi, so similarly was just a matter of some adjustment rather than requiring a major re-examination for her.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:01:34-08:00","id":818809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818803#post818803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I am married and we have mischief options, as long as we follow some rules, so I don't foresee any other long term partners (unless tragedy happens or we both fall in love with the same person) but short term could come up. My wife is Bi, so similarly was just a matter of some adjustment rather than requiring a major re-examination for her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much same here, except we're not married yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:54:03-08:00","id":819193,"title":"","content":"Well, thanks for the answers and even more for the personal testimonies. I think I understand it now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T15:56:01-08:00","id":825136,"title":"","content":"So I have a question, and it's probably stupid but here it goes.<br /> <br /> Which trans celebrity is the most respected in the trans community? I ask because cis folks like myself make a big deal out of Caitlyn Jenner, but I've heard that some trans people don't like her because she's a republican despite how horrible republicans are on LGBT issues.<br /> <br /> So basically my question is, what trans celebrities do trans people actually like, and what's your personal ranking of trans celebrities in regards to not being someone who has betrayed the trans community? (and as a future Savannah resident, where does Lady Chablis fall on the list?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 02-06-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T16:39:21-08:00","id":825150,"title":"","content":"I don't really... err... Know any trans celebrities. I follow a few trans people on Tumblr who are very popular there, but I don't think that counts. That said, I've got no beef with Caitlyn Jenner. I don't agree with her political views, but I respect her as a trans woman who came out despite having been in the public eye before transitioning. She doesn't speak for me as a trans woman, but good on her for what she did for herself.<br /> <br /> That's just the thing though, and forgive me if this is a slight deviation from your question, but... She's famous for her football career. She became a celebrity before she was out, and then when she came out the media just kind of had to deal with the fact that a person who was already a celebrity was also trans. Openly trans people don't tend to get to her level of fame. Even in media <i>about</i> trans people casts cis actors in trans roles more often than not. That's a big part of why I <i>can't</i> be openly trans in real life. I work in theater and it would pretty much be career suicide. I can't really name trans celebrities I like because there's not many to chose from, and that speaks to the huge issue with trans representation in media.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T17:00:30-08:00","id":825157,"title":"","content":"If I had to pick one trans person who is semi famous to call my favorite it would be Jazz Jennings. She is a young trans girl who has regular videos on you tube and a childrens book about her life. She deals with her issues and problems and speaks from her heart. <br /> <br /> Other ones of note are Jamie Clayton who stars in netflix series Sense 8 and the filk musician Alexander James Adams, who spent 20 years creating music as Heather Alexander before realizing that he could not tell people to live there true and honest lives when denying there own truth.<br /> <br /> I will try and keep a eye on this thread and answer questions as they show up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T17:57:42-08:00","id":825166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=825150#post825150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just the thing though, and forgive me if this is a slight deviation from your question, but... She's famous for her football career. She became a celebrity before she was out, and then when she came out the media just kind of had to deal with the fact that a person who was already a celebrity was also trans. Openly trans people don't tend to get to her level of fame. Even in media <i>about</i> trans people casts cis actors in trans roles more often than not. That's a big part of why I <i>can't</i> be openly trans in real life. I work in theater and it would pretty much be career suicide. I can't really name trans celebrities I like because there's not many to chose from, and that speaks to the huge issue with trans representation in media.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't realize things were that bad for trans actors and actresses. I have a trans character in my novel series I am working and since I am writing it with movie adaptions in mind, I suppose I should take that into account... I would prefer to have an actual trans actress cast, at least for the post transition version of her in the modern plot line where she first appears. There's also a flashback plot line in each book starting in the 60s, a closeted pre-transition version of her is one of the main heroes of the 90s segment of the flashback plot in the last segment of the series I have planned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T18:06:03-08:00","id":825170,"title":"","content":"Laverne Cox and Jazz Jennings come to mind. I follow Lesbian/Bi famous people more closely than trans, but as far as trans go those two leap to mind.<br /> <br /> But mostly anyone but Caitlyn Jenner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T18:15:15-08:00","id":825173,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answers. I'll have to watch some of the thing these ladies are in. Alas, none them have quite the phenotype I'm looking for the trans character in my novel, meaning I envision her as having a darker Latina appearance. Then again, who knows? Maybe there will be a famous trans Latina actress by the time my novels get a movie adaption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T18:30:55-08:00","id":825179,"title":"","content":"Laverne Cox and Jazz Jennings are there... Caitlyn Jenner is... like, I get why she says some of the stuff she does. But she's very much someone who was very fortunate to have the money and power to get past some of the things a lot of other trans people (especially those who aren't white) have to deal with and... she doesn't always seem to &quot;get&quot; that?<br /> <br /> On the actor issue... it's worse than that because not only do they hire cis people to play trans parts more often than not, they hire people of the opposite gender, and act like there are no trans actors. It's... a sore point for me and at least some people I know.<br /> <br /> Oh, there's one who I'm going to menion because while she has been dead since the 90s, she created some technology that I suspect most of us use on a daily basis for a video game she made, Danielle Bunten. She made MULE, Seven Cities of Gold (the game in question needed more information than the computers of the time could hold in RAM, and so she developed a real time streaming code that'd let it work), HQ Commander (as an interesting note, she had the choice of this or making a little known game Civilization, and Sid Meier convinced her to take that one), and others... she was big on multiplayer games back in the time when computers used 5.25 inch floppies... FLOPPIES!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T19:31:14-08:00","id":825201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=825136#post825136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask because cis folks like myself make a big deal out of Caitlyn Jenner, but I've heard that some trans people don't like her because she's a republican despite how horrible republicans are on LGBT issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more complicated than that. Here's a nice rant on Caitlyn and why transfolk dislike her:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://kinfolkkollective.com/2015/11/16/call-her-out-but-call-her-cait-caitlyn-jenner-and-why-im-never-here-for-transphobi/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://kinfolkkollective.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/KUBET-\u0e04\u0e32\u0e2a\u0e34\u0e42\u0e19\u0e2d\u0e2d\u0e19\u0e44\u0e25\u0e19\u0e4c\u0e17\u0e35\u0e48\u0e14\u0e35\u0e17\u0e35\u0e48\u0e2a\u0e38\u0e14\u0e43\u0e19\u0e40\u0e2d\u0e40\u0e0a\u0e35\u0e22.webp\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://kinfolkkollective.com/2015/11/16/call-her-out-but-call-her-cait-caitlyn-jenner-and-why-im-never-here-for-transphobi/\" target=\"_blank\"> KUBET \u0e40\u0e27\u0e47\u0e1a\u0e1e\u0e19\u0e31\u0e19\u0e04\u0e32\u0e2a\u0e34\u0e42\u0e19\u0e2a\u0e25\u0e47\u0e2d\u0e15\u0e41\u0e17\u0e07\u0e1a\u0e2d\u0e25\u0e2d\u0e2d\u0e19\u0e44\u0e25\u0e19\u0e4c \u0e22\u0e2d\u0e14\u0e19\u0e34\u0e22\u0e21 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://kinfolkkollective.com/2015/11/16/call-her-out-but-call-her-cait-caitlyn-jenner-and-why-im-never-here-for-transphobi/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://kinfolkkollective.com/2015/11/16/call-her-out-but-call-her-cait-caitlyn-jenner-and-why-im-never-here-for-transphobi/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \u0e17\u0e35\u0e48\u0e2a\u0e38\u0e14\u0e02\u0e2d\u0e07\u0e04\u0e27\u0e32\u0e21\u0e2a\u0e19\u0e38\u0e01 \u0e40\u0e25\u0e48\u0e19\u0e07\u0e48\u0e32\u0e22\u0e44\u0e14\u0e49\u0e40\u0e07\u0e34\u0e19\u0e08\u0e23\u0e34\u0e07 \u0e40\u0e25\u0e48\u0e19\u0e21\u0e31\u0e19\u0e2a\u0e4c\u0e17\u0e38\u0e01\u0e27\u0e31\u0e19 \u0e01\u0e31\u0e1a KUBET \u0e40\u0e27\u0e47\u0e1a\u0e1e\u0e19\u0e31\u0e19\u0e2d\u0e2d\u0e19\u0e44\u0e25\u0e19\u0e4c\u0e17\u0e35\u0e48\u0e40\u0e25\u0e48\u0e19\u0e07\u0e48\u0e32\u0e22\u0e44\u0e14\u0e49\u0e40\u0e07\u0e34\u0e19\u0e08\u0e23\u0e34\u0e07 \u0e40\u0e15\u0e34\u0e21\u0e40\u0e15\u0e47\u0e21\u0e04\u0e27\u0e32\u0e21\u0e21\u0e31\u0e19\u0e2a\u0e4c\u0e44\u0e14\u0e49\u0e41\u0e1a\u0e1a\u0e44\u0e21\u0e48\u0e21\u0e35\u0e17\u0e35\u0e48\u0e2a\u0e34\u0e49\u0e19\u0e2a\u0e38\u0e14 </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T23:32:41-08:00","id":825293,"title":"","content":"The first rule of being transgender, a rule I break far to often for my own emotional health. Don't read the comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:07:05-08:00","id":825375,"title":"","content":"Though sometimes you find comments that are happy. Like some comments I saw about the girl scout whose neighbor having transphobic nature and being mean to her resulted in support from her mom and thousands of other people. But generally, yeah...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:28:41-08:00","id":825688,"title":"","content":"A minor internet celebrity I am peripherally aware of has come out as trans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n2He0zJgNak\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n2He0zJgNak\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n2He0zJgNak\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n2He0zJgNak </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I genuinely had no idea an inability to eat without gagging could be a symptom of dysmorphia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T22:45:16-08:00","id":826578,"title":"","content":"So one thing I always wonder, how often do you find you need to explain your status to new people? I know it can get tiring.<br /> <br /> One of my Players is transgender and he is so much happier not having to pretend to be a &quot;girl&quot; at work, as we are coworkers, and just chill. Its funny RPGs seem big with the LGBT community, and over all my groups I've had 3 players that have lived the transgender experience.<br /> <br /> I would imagine it beneath ones dignity to deny ones nature for sake of dodging Workplace or professional hardships.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for do people think of themselves as a gender all the time, well the concept of gender seems imposed on me I only grew up existing where Sex was important factor, seconded by what people prefer to be called.<br /> <br /> Well cheers to you all, it is a haaaard path, and any path requiring eternal medicine regiments would not be for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:13:44-08:00","id":826584,"title":"","content":"I came out once to my inlaws, once to my family, and in a giant email to my players. I try to now broadcast my gender as much as possible. I came out when trans persons were hitting the radar, which means I have had less explaining to do. People who transitioned even 5 years ago no doubt had more explaining to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:16:53-08:00","id":826585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826578#post826578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine it beneath ones dignity to deny ones nature for sake of dodging Workplace or professional hardships.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, frankly, a pretty uncool thing to say, considering I <i>just</i> posted on this same page that my profession is the biggest reason I can't be out in my day-to-day life.<br /> <br /> I don't &quot;deny my nature&quot;, I know exactly who I am. Part of who I am is an actor, an if I started taking steps to transition, I would no longer be castable in male roles. Breasts are kind of a barrier to that. I would most likely not suddenly become castable in female roles, because I don't fit within the box of classic &quot;feminine beauty&quot;. While I may be perfectly confident in my own appearance, that means precisely fuck all when it comes to casting. Between my baritone voice, my prominent Adam's apple, and my masculine facial features, no director is going to want me to play the romantic lead. It's not like I can afford extensive cosmetic surgery on the pittance I make as an actor, so that pretty much means I'd cut myself off from any roles besides trans women. Now, there are not a lot of trans roles out there to begin with, and a good portion of them I would <i>not</i> want to play because they are pretty much a big pile of harmful stereotypes. The few that are actually well written are mostly going to be in the kind of artsy shows that don't draw a big audience, and the kinds of theaters that are going to produce them often can't afford to pay much. And <i>on top of all of that,</i> directors usually cast cis men in trans woman roles. Fuck, I could probably get cast as a trans woman <i>more easily</i> by staying in the closet.<br /> <br /> So no, it's not beneath my dignaty to stay closeted in my professional life. It's a practical concern that if I want to eat, I've got to keep passing as male. That, or find another career, but that's what I like doing, it's what I'm good at doing, and it's just as much a part of my identity as being trans is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I apologize if I come off a little harsh here. It was not my intention to snap at you, it's just a very personal subject for me and your comment just happened to touch a bit of a nerve. I'm going to leave it here, because I think it's stuff that's worth being said, but please know that I don't mean the rant to be directed at you. More than anything, it's a stream of consciousness about stuff that I constantly have to deal with but very rarely talk about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-09-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:27:05-08:00","id":826590,"title":"","content":"I apologize for my ungraceful post, I didn't read the entire thread yet. I was just meaning I see a lot of stress on my friend having to straddle the line, and it gets confusing calling him a her at work but not at work. I just feel my friend should feel comfortable being who he is without feeling prejudiced or harassed. He's Hard working and says jugging three jobs and being three people is stressful. I also feel that it is unnecessary because our job already has hired transgendered individuals. I even convinced him to do a seasonal job and he got to be he there because it was a comfortable atmosphere.<br /> <br /> But I sincerely apologize Charlaquin, I'm an irascible clod sometimes. I admit it, I try not offend people. It can be a precarious line when one doesn't know the context of new friends and coworkers lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:29:57-08:00","id":826593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826584#post826584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came out once to my inlaws, once to my family, and in a giant email to my players. I try to now broadcast my gender as much as possible. I came out when trans persons were hitting the radar, which means I have had less explaining to do. People who transitioned even 5 years ago no doubt had more explaining to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember like a Decade ago most people didn't even know the term Transgender was a thing. It seems with the idea of being an actual &quot;thing&quot;, an actual option has resulted in lots of young people I know reshape their identity. I can't imagine coming out in say the 90s!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:31:37-08:00","id":826595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826590#post826590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize for my ungraceful post, I didn't read the entire thread yet. I was just meaning I see a lot of stress on my friend having to straddle the line, and it gets confusing calling him a her at work but not at work. I just feel my friend should feel comfortable being who he is without feeling prejudiced or harassed. He's Hard working and says jugging three jobs and being three people is stressful. I also feel that it is unnecessary because our job already has hired transgendered individuals. I even convinced him to do a seasonal job and he got to be he there because it was a comfortable atmosphere.<br /> <br /> But I sincerely apologize Charlaquin, I'm an irascible clod sometimes. I admit it, I try not offend people. It can be a precarious line when one doesn't know the context of new friends and coworkers lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I'm sure you didn't mean it to be hurtful, and this is a space specifically for asking questions about sensitive stuff. I'm sorry you ended up on the receiving end of a rant that really has more to do with my issues with the industry I work in than about anything you said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:39:22-08:00","id":826604,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine the Industry! Man I would enjoy being a Voice actor or work on Youtube Shows but I just hear its hella hard and if you have to go all in to make it.<br /> <br /> It feels to me growing up Kids are not taught that words like Midget and Tranny are hurtful words to some people, though I've had friends gleefully embrace tranny as title. I mean it seemed it was corrected within my lifetime not to use the term Retarded, unless talking specifically about Retarding aging or growth or Mental Retardation. Its just a mazy path. But seems at least the next generation hopefully will learn to be more sensitive. Though not tooooo sensitive hehe.<br /> <br /> I remember talking with a friend that was transgender and for a period and decided she felt better going back to her old path. She felt a lot of it had to do with culture not permitting people to show weakness, and I said I specifically try not to show obvious true weakness in the workplace due to the instinct of people frenzy at the smell of blood.<br /> <br /> I must sound like a crazy fella. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:03:02-08:00","id":826617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826593#post826593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember like a Decade ago most people didn't even know the term Transgender was a thing. It seems with the idea of being an actual &quot;thing&quot;, an actual option has resulted in lots of young people I know reshape their identity. I can't imagine coming out in say the 90s!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes I wish I had my realization and came out in college. Sometimes I wonder if I had come out in college if I would be alive now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:07:03-08:00","id":826618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826604#post826604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't imagine the Industry! Man I would enjoy being a Voice actor or work on Youtube Shows but I just hear its hella hard and if you have to go all in to make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's crazy rough. I'm very lucky in that I've found a steady, reliable job that allows me to do what I love with a flexible schedule (I work part time at a museum as an &quot;educator/performer&quot;) so if I hit a rough patch when I can't get work, or if I ever did decide I was going to transition and fuck what the industry thinks about it, I would actually be ok. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826604#post826604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels to me growing up Kids are not taught that words like Midget and Tranny are hurtful words to some people, though I've had friends gleefully embrace tranny as title. I mean it seemed it was corrected within my lifetime not to use the term Retarded, unless talking specifically about Retarding aging or growth or Mental Retardation. Its just a mazy path. But seems at least the next generation hopefully will learn to be more sensitive. Though not tooooo sensitive hehe.</div> </div> </div> </div>My parents actually had a great way of handling that. They taught me words aren't good or bad, words are just words, but there are two kinds of words that should be treated with great care. Some words, like fuck or shit, offend some people. You can usually tell whether or not those words are okay to use based on the situation and the kind of language the people there are using - if you hear someone else say &quot;fuck&quot; you know it's ok to say fuck around them. Then there are other words that have teeth and claws. Words like fat, stupid, ugly, any word that bullies use to make people feel bad about who they are. The thing about those words is that it doesn't matter if you're trying to use them to make someone feel bad or not. If you've been bullied by those words before, even hearing them in a different context can remind you of when you were hurt by them before, and it still hurts. Those words have teeth and claws, and they'll attack people even if that's not what you mean for them to do. You can never tell if someone around you has been hurt by one of those words before, or how badly, so it's almost always better just not to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:41:46-08:00","id":826632,"title":"","content":"I haven't had to come out to people very often, not after the flurry of outing myself to family, friend's and co-workers. Things went very fast after that, less than two weeks between my first public appearance as myself and living full time as me.<br /> <br /> People's reactions where very positive, only one or two of them acted weird for a while but they came around. Then again no one really seemed surprised, I knew I wasn't flawless in my act many people assumed I was gay. One of my favorite lines when I first started outing myself as trans was &quot;contrary to popular belief I do like women&quot; I do feel a bit cheated though, no one ever reacted with disbelief. It was all a mix of &quot;you got to do what makes you happy&quot; and &quot;ya I thought it was something like that&quot;<br /> <br /> After that initial flurry no one seems to ask, I spent a lot of time wondering if they know and are afraid to ask questions or if they don't realize I am trans. I have trouble believing that I ever pass, I see all my flaws, my voice is terrible, my body is all wrong. Or that's how I see it, when I am more objective it's not that bad and I can almost think someone might not know right away.<br /> <br /> Ok totally went off subject, I will say its nice to be answering questions, I told everyone when I came out to ask me questions and no one ever dose. I know that with most people they are just concerned with hurting my feelings and don't want to ask something offensive. Which is unlikely, the real danger I feel is someone asks a question and I give a TMI answer. :-P so really ask away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T01:31:51-08:00","id":826645,"title":"","content":"Yea I lucked out with my friends too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:17:56-08:00","id":826714,"title":"","content":"For my part, I've come out to most of my family, except my parents and I guess sister (well, I came out to my mother, but she either forgot/had pushed it out of mind/both, and said some terrible things, but not out of hate but a personal fear and pain) as well as my friends. My father is a huge bigot in many ways including homophobe, so... and my sister is the WAY religious conservative who once started a fight with a bi girlfriend on a personal blog of mine by saying homosexuality is evil and wrong, and I didn't stand for it either.<br /> <br /> I super lucked out with one friend. Even his wife wasn't sure how he'd take it, but he pretty much took it in stride if not getting it much at first. He obviously wanted to though. He is a caring person and we've been friends since my first year at uni. Pretty much all of my close friends know and a fair number were like &quot;Yeah, I kinda thought that was the case, but I didn't want to assume.&quot; The amusing one of those was when I met their trans nephew at the same weekend con. Who married a nice guy and I was there for them meeting. Kinda one of those happy stories.<br /> <br /> On the job issue, I know someone in the tech industry, and the way she puts it is... she doesn't hide it, but she doesn't put it out there either. They could find the information and she realizes it could hurt her to do them. There are others she knows at the same company who do hide, and she gets it.Tech as a woman is tough enough. Add in intersectionality and things get worse potentially. Even if people don't try to be bigoted, they might act badly.<br /> <br /> The group I've most regularly had... difficulty from was gay men. It's not been pretty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:05:55-08:00","id":826793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=818629#post818629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the attraction to a particular set of genitals that's the problem, it's the attraction to a particular set of genitals <i>on a person of a particular gender</i>. If you like dicks, that's one thing. If you like women who have dicks because that's not what cis women have, you're focused on how we're different from cis women, and that's what's transphobic about it. I don't want to be the object of attraction because I'm a dickgirl and that's so exotic and hot. I want to be a woman that you are attracted to or not according to your tastes, just like any other woman would be.<br /> <br /> (Note, I'm using the general form of you, not talking about anyone specifically).<br /> <br /> <br /> Chasers are people who fetishize trans people, which is a creepy and abusive thing to do. If you're talking about normal people who aren't abusive creeps, you're not talking about the same people I am.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think neither sexual arousal or grossed out are voluntary reactions, it your trans nature is a turn on to someone, then its not a choice on their part, same with being grossed out.<br /> <br /> Then again your feelings of being creeped out aren't voluntary either. But I would not confuse them with objective truth either.<br /> <br /> I think its how you treat people that matters more then your emotional reactions.<br /> <br /> For the record I have neither reaction to trans individuals.<br /> <br /> What's your thoughts on two spirit people, how do they fit within the trans community?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:44:18-08:00","id":826811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826793#post826793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think neither sexual arousal or grossed out are voluntary reactions, it your trans nature is a turn on to someone, then its not a choice on their part, same with being grossed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well, society doesn't function on involuntary impulses. What matters is how you act on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826793#post826793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again your feelings of being creeped out aren't voluntary either. But I would not confuse them with objective truth either.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, my feelings on the matter are conscious and reasoned. Of course they are my opinions, and not everyone shares them, but this is a thread about answering personal questions. Most of the answers herein are inherently going to be opinions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826793#post826793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think its how you treat people that matters more then your emotional reactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826793#post826793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record I have neither reaction to trans individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=826793#post826793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your thoughts on two spirit people, how do they fit within the trans community?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of two spirit is very closely tied to American First Nations culture, and claiming to be two spirit if you're not Native American smacks of cultural appropriation. Generally, non-native folks who identify with the concept of two souls would do better to research similar ideas that are less culturally specific, like bigender. For native people who identify as two spirit, that's that. I don't really have strong feelings about it, any more than I have strong feelings about any other gender identity. We are who we are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T12:57:22-08:00","id":827013,"title":"","content":"My knowledge of Two Spirits is exclusively very academic, so I have nothing firsthand to add.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:40:38-08:00","id":827105,"title":"","content":"I've never heard it brought up by any of the First Nations people I've met, even though they've shared with me a number of words and other cultural things... And frankly, I'm not entirely sure how much of that culturally has survived... I mean, not the rough concept, but understanding of concepts is shaped by your sensibilities. And the cultures (for better or worse or both) have changed. For an example... I was reading an article about the intent of the term &quot;natural-born citizen&quot;... which is almost certainly not what we would think of it as, because we live in a very different world from that of when it was written. The meaning to us is going to have none of the same emphasis by recent past and current events (for those who wrote it).<br /> <br /> It's human nature to view the world from your own place, even if realistically the things that made something important were super different back then. At best, we have educated guesses, but we don't KNOW.<br /> <br /> I'll also say I would see it as cultural appropriation if you took a term like that without... you know, being part of the culture, or at least having it in your family history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T00:47:53-08:00","id":828652,"title":"","content":"In the beginning outing seems to be all you're doing. I did family and close friends first, then the rest of my circle of friends and acquaintances, and lastly work.<br /> <br /> Especially work was scary. I work at the Benelux headquarters of a multinational, and first it was my manager, followed by my direct colleagues, then my department and finally a mail to every single one of the 600 people working here the weekend before I went to work presenting as a woman.<br /> <br /> All this outing took several months to get to everyone.<br /> <br /> And somewhat to my pleasant surprise, I have not had a single negative experience (at least to my face). On the contrary, even. I seriously lucked out :-)<br /> <br /> Nothing to add about the two spirit thing as I'm from Europe.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T00:38:48-08:00","id":829163,"title":"","content":"when I finally reached the point where I knew I had to transision I came out to a few close friends, after that I made a rule to come out to one new person each week, and that went on for several months before I sorta accidentally came out to everyone at once. I walked into my local game store during friday night magic busiest the store gets outside of huge events, wearing a floral skirt and simple black top. There was some hugging and positive reinforcement from those people who already knew, and some questions and weirdness from others but it all resolved itself quickly, especially because I didnt let it end there, for the next two weeks unless I was going to work I was presenting as myself and after those two weeks I was full time. I went from my first time out as myself to full time in 16 days. So the coming out thing was quick.<br /> <br /> One of the things that I have found remarkable is just how quickly things stop feeling new, diffrent, and special. When I first started being me it was constantly scary, exciting, nervous, half paniced happiness. By the second month everything just felt normal again, except some special situations like using the ladies room or similar gender specific situations and after 6 months or so even those feel normal. Even with friends, I had one who sorta freaked out. He was acting sorta like I died or something, it took about two months for him to get use to the change, to get used to the idea that even if my apperance was new I had not really changed much at all,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T23:53:17-07:00","id":898719,"title":"","content":"Well one of my transgender male friends is getting close to being assigned hormones and maybe chest surgery. I am wanting my friend to talk with another friend of mine who identified as male for a few years and went back to female. I'm nervous with things like hormone treatment and the like because I don't trust medical science to be as advanced as in comic books, but I told my friend it's his decision so I'll stick with him through it. He currently has a very thin physique, think waifish female model thin, but he wants to be a beardy male model and understands he will put on weight so will have to work make sure it's muscle instead of flab.<br /> <br /> I like my friend the way he is so I'm unsure on the medical gamble, but admittedly I am biased because I don't care about adding more masculinity to the world but I am chagrined at a loss of feminity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:49:44-07:00","id":899215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=898719#post898719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well one of my transgender male friends is getting close to being assigned hormones and maybe chest surgery. I am wanting my friend to talk with another friend of mine who identified as male for a few years and went back to female. I'm nervous with things like hormone treatment and the like because I don't trust medical science to be as advanced as in comic books, but I told my friend it's his decision so I'll stick with him through it. He currently has a very thin physique, think waifish female model thin, but he wants to be a beardy male model and understands he will put on weight so will have to work make sure it's muscle instead of flab.<br /> <br /> I like my friend the way he is so I'm unsure on the medical gamble, but admittedly I am biased because I don't care about adding more masculinity to the world but I am chagrined at a loss of feminity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your friend's gamble to make. He's profoundly unhappy and is willing to do something drastic to become who he really is, and he thinks the risks are worth it. All you can do is be there for him and not lament the &quot;loss of femininity&quot; or complain that you &quot;like him the way he is,&quot; because he rather clearly doesn't like the way he is and wants to change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:08:23-07:00","id":899565,"title":"","content":"Changing Subjects some: I have been rping for going on 20 years next year (and it all started with VtM revised) and I must ask: How do you handled transgendered characters (not players) at the table? I ask as this is a topic near and dear to my heart (I am a gay man who fights vehemently for the BTQAI part of the LGBT community against group ignorance that the mainstream LG community can and does propagate). I graduated from playing chainsaw Gangrel and beatstick Brujah with a transgendered Daughter of Cacophony who was desperately afraid the other DoCs would find out about her physical sex versus her true gender back in 2000 because a friend of mine came out as trans and I wanted to try to understand through a kind of immersion play. I asked my friend at the time all kinds of questions while she was exploring how she felt as a woman instead of the man she had been raised as. My character lasted a good year and change before my ST moved and I came to realize, through rp and my friend's struggles, how hateful the world could be to non-binary people.<br /> <br /> In my most current game I am running a character is being played as a thinblooded Tzimisce Koldun (house rules: Lose Animalism, Auspex, or Vicissitude for Koldunic Sorcery) who has no talent for Vicissitude but is hearing all kinds of rumors about how her clan can shape flesh and mold bodies to fit their desires and is going haywire in game trying to figure out what is &quot;wrong&quot; with her blood. The character is very well developed, I like the struggles of how she should have a supernatural &quot;get out of jail free&quot; card but does not, and the learning of that she's looked down upon by the Camarilla for her clan and lack of blood potency and not because she is transgender.<br /> <br /> As a gay male nerd, VtM always helped me with my self-esteem. I was odd (half-Asian male who liked men and gaming and rap and on and on) but in the WoD the LGBT community was not overshadowed, was not pushed aside, it was embraced. I remember the LGBT only packs of the Sabbat and the one in Montreal; Celeste from Nights of Prophecy (you stole my idea WW!), Troile and Moloch from Clanbook Baali (okay, let's ignore the opening fiction yeah? Yeah.)! I feel that the LGBT community and the World of Darkness are well tied together and have always been buddies while many other rpgs gloss over the ideas (D&amp;D) or are openly hostile to them (FATAL). But, to be fair, no one in their right mind plays FATAL.<br /> <br /> I think I may have rambled some: Anyway, not counting people who blatantly hamfist characters (My guy is a super flamboyant drag queen lolololol!) have you had any players who wanted to explore transgender and/or transsexual issues? Have you enjoyed such characters if you did? If any didn't seem to 'get' the concept did you encourage them to learn or shift their focus to another character type?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Debating between ghouls and hunters PbP","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11874-melora","name":"Melora","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:54:57-07:00","id":899590,"title":"","content":"Now that you mention it, I don't think I've had any cis players want to play trans characters. I have had players on various parts of the trans spectrum play characters on <i>other</i> parts of the spectrum many times, and have played a trans character once before. But most cis folks I've played with aren't really interested in playing trans characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T18:16:52-07:00","id":899611,"title":"","content":"That's interesting, because I've never seen anyone I know play a trans character, and I've only played one like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>. Though a close friend did have a once cis now trans changeling woman as well as someone who was obviously genderqueer as NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T22:43:49-07:00","id":899770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Melora</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=899565#post899565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, not counting people who blatantly hamfist characters (My guy is a super flamboyant drag queen lolololol!) have you had any players who wanted to explore transgender and/or transsexual issues? Have you enjoyed such characters if you did? If any didn't seem to 'get' the concept did you encourage them to learn or shift their focus to another character type?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In VTM, no. In one campaign of Werewolf, i did get a gal player who had her Kinfolk lorekeeper, who was L. In a few SW games, i have counted maybe 4 gay characters. As for Trangenders, not yet encountered a player wanting to go that route.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T01:50:07-07:00","id":899864,"title":"","content":"I've never played a trans character. My life is rough enough with it I play to escape. I have not had a player do so either. I have been told, in confidence, by a player that they would be a little uncomfortable plying one in a game with me as they would almost feel like they are trivializing it. I do have trans NPCs (one in Geist, two in Changeling, one in Demon so far) but not many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T07:16:07-07:00","id":900004,"title":"","content":"I've got a lot of transgender characters that I'm waiting to play, but I've been without a group for a few years how so they're likely to stay shelved for some time. As mentioned elsewhere, I'm currently very unsure about my gender identity, so it's telling that most of my new characters are some shade of queer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:13:47-07:00","id":900037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=899864#post899864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never played a trans character. My life is rough enough with it I play to escape. I have not had a player do so either. I have been told, in confidence, by a player that they would be a little uncomfortable plying one in a game with me as they would almost feel like they are trivializing it. I do have trans NPCs (one in Geist, two in Changeling, one in Demon so far) but not many.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I think it says something that the one trans character I made was only recently. And in a weird way, WoD game (specifically Mage 20) seems like... hopeful. Sure there are bad things for characters, but they're not the things I deal with. She lives in a sort of place where the trans part of her life can be happy, it's just other supernatural stuff that's problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:21:20-07:00","id":901392,"title":"","content":"So... I'm an idiot and forgot that this thread exists! I should have come here for the question. <br /> <br /> I'm running a Exalted Fan Survey and included a question on Gender and I am getting a lot of comments about it. What is the best way to ask the gender question so that it is inclusive for individuals of all genders?<br /> <br /> Here is how I worded the question:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://acidspiders.files.wordpress.com/2016/05/genderquestion.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:33:26-07:00","id":901406,"title":"","content":"That looks decently constructed. I would recommend changing the unmodified male and female to cis male and cis female, but knowing the exalted forum that would probably start another shitstorm.<br /> <br /> Another way to construct it that might be less alienating to trans people could be to break it into two separate questions. One that asks your gender and has male, female, non-binary, agender, or prefer not to specify as options, and another that asks if you are cis, trans, or prefer not to specify.<br /> <br /> Either way, I would recommend adding agender as an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:46:16-07:00","id":901420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=901406#post901406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That looks decently constructed. I would recommend changing the unmodified male and female to cis male and cis female, but knowing the exalted forum that would probably start another shitstorm.<br /> <br /> Another way to construct it that might be less alienating to trans people could be to break it into two separate questions. One that asks your gender and has male, female, non-binary, agender, or prefer not to specify as options, and another that asks if you are cis, trans, or prefer not to specify.<br /> <br /> Either way, I would recommend adding agender as an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will split the question for next year's survey. And add agender. <br /> <br /> Thanks for your help! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:57:03-07:00","id":901488,"title":"","content":"Might I also suggest bi-gender, since it means you have gender, and it's within the binary, but it doesn't fit under any of the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T16:52:52-07:00","id":901520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=901488#post901488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might I also suggest bi-gender, since it means you have gender, and it's within the binary, but it doesn't fit under any of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think bigender is pretty distinctly non-binary in spite of its name. It just means having two or more genders, those genders don't always conform to the gender binary though. At least, that's how my partner explains it, and they are bigender. <br /> <br /> Of course, I'm never opposed to more gender options on polls, so don't take my clarification as admonition of bigender as a poll option. Just expanding on the definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:04:04-07:00","id":901530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=901520#post901520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think bigender is pretty distinctly non-binary in spite of its name. It just means having two or more genders, those genders don't always conform to the gender binary though. At least, that's how my partner explains it, and they are bigender.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm never opposed to more gender options on polls, so don't take my clarification as admonition of bigender as a poll option. Just expanding on the definition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kinda what I figured. Because I've known people who say they are bigender but don't see themselves as outside the gender binary. I think it's one of those things. Like in the survey I said I identified as a woman, not trans woman. Because it's how I identify, and I feel vaguely annoyed at the way I don't have a choice how most see me. So it's part of me, but not how I identify. If that makes sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:01:11-07:00","id":901586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=901530#post901530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda what I figured. Because I've known people who say they are bigender but don't see themselves as outside the gender binary. I think it's one of those things. Like in the survey I said I identified as a woman, not trans woman. Because it's how I identify, and I feel vaguely annoyed at the way I don't have a choice how most see me. So it's part of me, but not how I identify. If that makes sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally understandable. Conversely, I would select non-binary and trans because for me transness is a big part of my identity, but I don't think it would be entirely accurate for me to identify as female in the poll, as while I trend feminine and prefer she/her pronouns, I don't identify as strictly female, nor do I typically experience many of the same struggles most women (cis or trans) face.<br /> <br /> That's why I recommended splitting the questions between what gender you are and whether you are cis, trans, or prefer not to choose one or the other. It's more granular and allows for a greater number of people to select options that resonate with them.<br /> <br /> I would also toss out the word &quot;Identify&quot; and ask &quot;what gender <i>are</i> you?&quot; to avoid implying (even if unintentionally) that you're not <i>really</i> [whatever gender], you just <i>identify</i> that way, and to avoid baiting responses of &quot;I identify as an attack hellicopter.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:53:46-07:00","id":901625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=901586#post901586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally understandable. Conversely, I would select non-binary and trans because for me transness is a big part of my identity, but I don't think it would be entirely accurate for me to identify as female in the poll, as while I trend feminine and prefer she/her pronouns, I don't identify as strictly female, nor do I typically experience many of the same struggles most women (cis or trans) face.<br /> <br /> That's why I recommended splitting the questions between what gender you are and whether you are cis, trans, or prefer not to choose one or the other. It's more granular and allows for a greater number of people to select options that resonate with them.<br /> <br /> I would also toss out the word &quot;Identify&quot; and ask &quot;what gender <i>are</i> you?&quot; to avoid implying (even if unintentionally) that you're not <i>really</i> [whatever gender], you just <i>identify</i> that way, and to avoid baiting responses of &quot;I identify as an attack hellicopter.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is one of those things why it's useful to have multiple things to allow people more choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T21:09:03-07:00","id":901710,"title":"","content":"I always just fill in female unless I think I might have sex with someone in the forum/conversation. Transness is my business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T09:38:31-07:00","id":908394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=898719#post898719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like my friend the way he is so I'm unsure on the medical gamble, but admittedly I am biased because I don't care about adding more masculinity to the world but I am chagrined at a loss of feminity.</div> </div> </div> </div> As a man I find that insulting, masculinity is a wonderful thing (as is feminity), its not of lesser value then feminity.<br /> <br /> This clearly bothers you not for medical reasons, but because you've been taught that men and maculinity are bad.<br /> <br /> There is more to maculinity then violence, hell feminity can be violent too.<br /> <br /> Maculinity builds cities, cures disease, and all kinds of cool stuff.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong feminity can be awesome as well, and as Pagan I try to cultivate both according what fits me as a man.<br /> <br /> I wish your friend luck, your friend will have unique challenge, but will also have a chance to explore masculinity with fresh eyes. Its a huge opportunity to grow as a person, and be truer to who your friend feels to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 06-06-2016, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T00:32:29-07:00","id":912136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=908394#post908394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a man I find that insulting, masculinity is a wonderful thing (as is feminity), its not of lesser value then feminity.<br /> <br /> This clearly bothers you not for medical reasons, but because you've been taught that men and maculinity are bad.<br /> <br /> There is more to maculinity then violence, hell feminity can be violent too.<br /> <br /> Maculinity builds cities, cures disease, and all kinds of cool stuff.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong feminity can be awesome as well, and as Pagan I try to cultivate both according what fits me as a man.<br /> <br /> I wish your friend luck, your friend will have unique challenge, but will also have a chance to explore masculinity with fresh eyes. Its a huge opportunity to grow as a person, and be truer to who your friend feels to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gender is a social construct whose absurdity is very quickly exposed when you replace labels with the one word that actually defines us all: Human.<br /> <br /> There is more to *Humanity than violence, hell *humanity can be violent too<br /> *Humanity builds cities, cures diseases, and all kids of cool stuff.<br /> *Don't get me wrong, *humanity* can be awesome as well, and as a *human I try to cultivate both according to what fits me as a *human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{