Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-11-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T02:26:56-07:00","id":917256,"title":"","content":"i have a few questions.<br /> <br /> 1) is it possible to be both transgender and gay at the sametime?<br /> <br /> 2)likewise is it true that thansgender people are more fluid in their sexual orientation?<br /> <br /> 3)i didn't read the entire thread but...from what i did read as well as other sources is there some hostility between some gay men and transgender men/women?<br /> <br /> 4) how does it feel to be transgender? i just have difficulty understanding it other than on an intellectual level. for instance does a transgender woman instictively dislike having male genitals?<br /> even if she has never seen female ones(young children i mean)<br /> <br /> <br /> if any of these sounded offensive i apologise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T02:38:26-07:00","id":917261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=917256#post917256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i have a few questions.<br /> <br /> 1) is it possible to be both transgender and gay at the sametime?<br /> <br /> 2)likewise is it true that thansgender people are more fluid in their sexual orientation?<br /> <br /> 3)i didn't read the entire thread but...from what i did read as well as other sources is there some hostility between some gay men and transgender men/women?<br /> <br /> 4) how does it feel to be transgender? i just have difficulty understanding it other than on an intellectual level. for instance does a transgender woman instictively dislike having male genitals?<br /> even if she has never seen female ones(young children i mean)<br /> <br /> <br /> if any of these sounded offensive i apologise</div> </div> </div> </div>1: Yes, a transgender man who desires male companionship is gay, just the same as a transgender woman who desires men is straight.<br /> <br /> 2: That's one hell of a blanket statement.<br /> <br /> 3 and 4 are more than I have in me to answer right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T04:01:09-07:00","id":917278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=917256#post917256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i have a few questions.<br /> <br /> 1) is it possible to be both transgender and gay at the sametime?<br /> <br /> 2)likewise is it true that thansgender people are more fluid in their sexual orientation?<br /> <br /> 3)i didn't read the entire thread but...from what i did read as well as other sources is there some hostility between some gay men and transgender men/women?<br /> <br /> 4) how does it feel to be transgender? i just have difficulty understanding it other than on an intellectual level. for instance does a transgender woman instictively dislike having male genitals?<br /> even if she has never seen female ones(young children i mean)<br /> <br /> <br /> if any of these sounded offensive i apologise</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Yes<br /> <br /> 2) Agreed it's a blanket statement. I think it's more, at most, they <b>might</b><b> be</b> more willing to be truthful with themselves about changes in it.<br /> <br /> 3) Kinda? I think it's more that there is a larger sort of group inside gay men (and also lesbians) who are well enough off, cis, white, and getting what they want more than other groups who are inconsiderate towards other members of the LGBTQAI community. Like say homeless and/or non-white youths who they want forcibly moved away from them. Or erasure of their part in movements (see how much is mentioned about Stonewall). Or just personally bad acts towards those people. It's not all of them, but it is a problem, and one I've seen a few gay friends who otherwise could fit into those groups admit isn't something they want to see go on. For an example, the HRC in the past. One of those friends talked about how they were suddenly mentioning trans people and they must be feeling like they need more people to give them support/money.<br /> <br /> 4) Sorry, I don't think you're trying to be offensive, but I too don't exactly have it in me to answer this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T07:04:29-07:00","id":917325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=917256#post917256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) is it possible to be both transgender and gay at the sametime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=917256#post917256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2)likewise is it true that thansgender people are more fluid in their sexual orientation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to echo the &quot;blanket statement&quot; sentiment. Trans people are too many and too varied for such an assertion to be meaningful. Most trans people deal with issues of sex and sexuality quite often, so it's fairly common for trans people to be extremely secure about such issues, but that doesn't necessarily mean being more fluid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=917256#post917256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3)i didn't read the entire thread but...from what i did read as well as other sources is there some hostility between some gay men and transgender men/women?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a complicated issue. Trans erasure is a big problem within the gay community, which can be a cause of animosity. There's also the issue of gay cis men excluding gay trans men, and gay cis men who will only consider other cis men as romantic and/or sexual partners. But really, these issues aren't by any means exclusive to the gay community.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=917256#post917256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) how does it feel to be transgender? i just have difficulty understanding it other than on an intellectual level. for instance does a transgender woman instictively dislike having male genitals?<br /> even if she has never seen female ones(young children i mean)</div> </div> </div> </div>Real quick before I try to answer this, I just want to point out that &quot;male genitals&quot; and &quot;female genitals&quot; are very cis-centric phrases, implying that certain sexual organs are intrinsically linked to certain genders. It's really better just to say penis or vagina if that's what you mean.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to attempt to answer this, many trans people do feel uncomfortable with their bodies, often including their genitals. This is called dysmorphia. Not all trans people experience dysmorphia, and it is experienced to different degrees and about different parts of the body for different people. Trans people also aren't the only people who experience dysmorphia - for example, some people have experienced feelings of body parts &quot;not belonging to them&quot; after surgery, that's another form of dysmorphia. Basically, feelings of one's body being wrong, or not the way it's supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Dysphoria is another common experience for trans people, possibly more common than dysmorphia. Rather than feeling uncomfortable with one's body, dysphoria is a feeling of discomfort with one's gender. The best way I could describe it is an intense discomfort in being thought of or treated as a certain gender. To help understand this, think about how young boys will often call each other girls or sissies as a bullying tactic (really, adult men do it too, they just tend to say &quot;bitch&quot; or &quot;pussy&quot; rather than &quot;girl&quot; or &quot;sissy&quot;). If you've ever experienced that and felt uncomfortable or ashamed to be treated that way, that's like a very small, short-lived example of dysphoria. For many trans people, that feeling is near constant.<br /> <br /> Of course, not all trans people experience dysphoria either. For some, their bodies and the genders they were assigned at birth aren't uncomfortable, but being thought of as a different gender makes them much happier. This was the case with me. Even before really knowing specifics about anatomical differences between sexes, it just made me happy when grown ups assumed I was a girl because I had long hair. I would find myself envying a lot of the clothes girls could wear that boys weren't supposed to. I knew my parents would have gotten me a dress or whatever if I asked, but I also knew I would get made fun of if I wore one at school, so I didn't. When ever it was an option in video games and things, I would choose a female avatar because it made me happy to know that the game thought of me as a girl.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=917256#post917256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if any of these sounded offensive i apologise</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that's what the thread is for. It's clear that offense is not your intent, and these kinds of questions can be really difficult to find answers to because there just aren't a lot of opportunities where it's appropriate to ask them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-19-2016, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T07:25:08-07:00","id":917337,"title":"","content":"And really, for the record, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> said, this is not exclusive to the trans community. There are a lot of parts that are erased or treated unwell. Bi erasure for one. If you're in a monogamous heterosexual relationship, you're considered straight. Monogamous gay, then you're just gay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T14:41:31-07:00","id":917563,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I apologize for even bringing this up, but I want to be 100% clear that Mark's suspension is not in any way a reflection of his actions in this thread. He is under no scrutiny for his comments, which given the nature of the thread were acceptable. This post does not mean discussing it is okay here.</span></b></span><br /> <br /> I'll be replying tonight. On phone now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:39:36-07:00","id":917584,"title":"","content":"Some are redundant, but I have a moment<br /> <br /> &quot;1) is it possible to be both transgender and gay at the sametime?&quot; <br /> <br /> Absolutely. I identify even more strongly as a lesbian than transgender. If someone asked me to summarize myself in three words it would be &quot;Lesbian, Gamer, Goth&quot; in that order. Only if I got more would you see &quot;Writer, Transgender Woman, Kinkster, Theist&quot; or whatever. When I watch a show or a move, I am immediately interested in queer female characters, and a lesbian is going to be a bigger sell than a trans women (unless she is also a lesbian, in which case redundant with the first half). <br /> <br /> &quot;2)likewise is it true that thansgender people are more fluid in their sexual orientation?&quot;<br /> <br /> I would say transgender people are not, but being people who are exploring themselves, those Kinsey 1s and 2s (or 4s and 5s) realize their flexibility in greater numbers. Many people don't realize how flexible their sexuality is because they have little to compare to for normal. Which is changing, but Transgender people are already upended. They have nothing to lose by exploring. <br /> <br /> &quot;3)i didn't read the entire thread but...from what i did read as well as other sources is there some hostility between some gay men and transgender men/women?&quot;<br /> <br /> To some degree. A lot of this is covered, but I have comments. A lot have been focused on how a lot of queer groups focus on gay men, and even lesbian culture excludes bi or pan women (honestly it is my experience at this point lesbian culture if more trans friendly than bi/pan friendly, but experiences vary). There is a lot of hostility from some trans circles because of this.<br /> <br /> Some gays don't like trans people because (some of us) don't blend easily and to them make acceptance more difficult. There is an element of the gay community who pushes against assimilation (the gay pride vs. gay shame argument) but most (especially younger) just want to be people. I suspect at this point this latter is a shrinking minority.<br /> <br /> There is also issues with Stonewall. Mainly, whether many of the persons who were most important in the conflict were gay drag queens or straight transgender women. Both sides have dug in claiming certain people, like Marsha P. Johnson and Sylvia Rivera. The fact is, culture was different then, and the lines were severely blurred between trans women and drag queens, or even hyperbutch women and trans men. As queer people have had to hide less and communicate more, there has come to be more differentiation between men who feel comfortable as men and love to be a character (and prefer female pronouns in character) and women who were identified at birth as men but are women 24/7, or want to be but have to try to disguise as men to protect themselves. These people were heroes to the queer community, and both sides want that hero to be one of us. Given several are dead now, including both above, we can't ask them. <br /> <br /> Some trans women really feel a strong dislike for drag queens, and the feeling is sometimes mutual. many of us feel the drag queens are making fun of us. Frankly, some are. But they have been a part of gay male culture for some time. This also leads to citing the drag queens at stonewall, trans people saying that is us, and a whole lot of punching instead of fucking, which is never the way to go. Regardless, drag queens can be a source of tension between gay men and trans women.<br /> <br /> I dunno if the gay male community has this issue, but in the lesbian community there are those who feel that trans men are being &quot;stolen&quot; from the lesbian community, that they would be happy as butch dykes for the Kinsey 6 ladies to enjoy at one time (and remember, some elements of the lesbian community fucking punish bi and trans women), and all this claptrap about transgender people are making the community &quot;lose&quot; them, as many women are not interested in (for example) anyone whose pheromones say man. Talk of &quot;bleeding out butches&quot; robs trans men of a voice, and discounts their experiences and feelings.<br /> <br /> \u200bSimilarly there is some (but shrinking) issues with female spaces. Obviously trans women, being women, deserve (and in many cases need) access to such spaces. Including bathrooms, women's shelters, and similar protected places. (I say bathrooms but shrinking as this has been a bigger issue with straight people than queer) Many of the same women who erase trans men's identity see trans women as men trying to get access to spaces...to see tits, I guess? I am pretty sure their own are they only tits most straight trans women care about. Anyway, some people, especially a number of second wave feminists, believe that trans women are invaders, and these TERFS are a problem.<br /> <br /> Now the gay male community might have issues like these? I find myself moving in female circles, not male. I know about the Stonewall issues but not much past that.<br /> <br /> This is not touching &quot;Should trans men have access to female spaces&quot; I lean toward no there, because I don't want men in female spaces more than cisgender women do. I have found some trans men do want access to female spaces, though. My mind is not settled on the matter. <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;4) how does it feel to be transgender? i just have difficulty understanding it other than on an intellectual level. for instance does a transgender woman instictively dislike having male genitals?<br /> even if she has never seen female ones(young children i mean)&quot;<br /> <br /> I am running out of time (Christ I am a blowhard), but I can say the answer is yes, some do, and no, some don't. Dysphoria and Dysmorphia are covered well by Charlaquen just above, and I am running out of time.<br /> <br /> And I was not offended by your questions. This is the place to post them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:03:02-07:00","id":918858,"title":"","content":"This thread as been a wonderful read. I feel honored to be part of the kind of community that is able to have such mature and respectful discussions.<br /> <br /> If I may add one little, maybe stupid, question:<br /> <br /> What are your opinions on non-binary/neutral neological pronouns? (IE. Ze in addition to He/She)<br /> <br /> My native tongue is french and I have read that there has been some talk of adding such a pronoun(s) to french. Yol, ol, ille and many others have been proposed.<br /> Since french grammar has nouns and adjective agree with pronouns, (La table/The table is feminine, but Le mur/The wall is masculine, etc.), it might be slightly more difficult than in english.<br /> <br /> Thank you all for taking the time to enlighten us, it's the only way to move towards a world free of outdated notions such as gender binarity.<br /> <br /> If it matters, I am a cisgender heterosexual male.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;La Victoire ou la Mort!&quot;<br /> <br /> Motto of the &quot;Les Fils du Nord&quot; clan","edited":{"userid":1100,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1100-malkenkaas","user":"MalkenKaas","date":"06-24-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1100-malkenkaas","name":"MalkenKaas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1100_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:30:31-07:00","id":918877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkenKaas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=918858#post918858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are your opinions on non-binary/neutral neological pronouns? (IE. Ze in addition to He/She)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's valuable to have gender neutral pronouns. Personally, I prefer They/Them because I'm more used to the way it sounds, but I'll use what ever pronouns someone tells me they prefer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkenKaas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=918858#post918858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My native tongue is french and I have read that there has been some talk of adding such a pronoun(s) to french. Yol, ol, ille and many others have been proposed.<br /> Since french grammar has nouns and adjective agree with pronouns, (La table/The table is feminine, but Le mur/The wall is masculine, etc.), it might be slightly more difficult than in english.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound like it would be more difficult to implement than in English. Glad to here that it's still being considered though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T18:20:04-07:00","id":918889,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1100-malkenkaas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1100_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1100\" data-vbnamecard=\"1100\">MalkenKaas</a> Truth be told, I'm not sold on nonstandard pronuns. Everyone I know who falls outside the binary has been perfectly fine with They/Them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T19:14:25-07:00","id":918907,"title":"","content":"I personally think they are very useful, but personally, I prefer They/Them also.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T20:16:54-07:00","id":918926,"title":"","content":"I am not a fan of nonbinary pronouns, beyond they/them. I will use them when asked, and respect those who desire it. I myself am very very binary though, downright girly.<br /> <br /> I did add an NPC to my Changeling game who is nonbinary in part to give me experience using them, and ze is a popular character with my group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T11:34:59-07:00","id":948717,"title":"","content":"I'm currently doing a bit of research on gender transition (for writing, not for myself), and I've been trying to figure out how long it would take on average to undergo a full physical transition. I've seen claims of two years, five, close to ten and anywhere in between. How long does a physical transition roughly take, given that everything goes well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T11:41:46-07:00","id":948719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=948717#post948717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently doing a bit of research on gender transition (for writing, not for myself), and I've been trying to figure out how long it would take on average to undergo a full physical transition. I've seen claims of two years, five, close to ten and anywhere in between. How long does a physical transition roughly take, given that everything goes well?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can think of hormone replacement therapy as a second puberty. As with the first puberty, it takes different amounts of time for different people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:28:20-07:00","id":948746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=948719#post948719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can think of hormone replacement therapy as a second puberty. As with the first puberty, it takes different amounts of time for different people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give or take five years, then?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:38:35-07:00","id":948755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=948746#post948746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give or take five years, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a reasonable ballpark estimate. And that's just for HRT. Depending on what a person wants to have done as part of their transition, they may require recovery time from surgery as well. Some people undergo lazer hair removal, which can take a very long time depending on how much you want removed. There's a lot of variables that can affect the length of transition, if you even want to put bookends on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:44:37-07:00","id":948764,"title":"","content":"And that's all assuming everything goes well. I have known people for whom the treatment was wasted or done wrong. Frankly, it's almost never just 5 years, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:47:35-07:00","id":948769,"title":"","content":"For contrast, I have a friend online who's only been on HRT for one year and has done nothing else, and she is perfectly passing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:59:10-07:00","id":948784,"title":"","content":"I'd been told for Hormones to do their thing 3-7 years, weighted very heavily on the higher number. And if/whens on things like surgery and laser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T11:18:57-07:00","id":952631,"title":"","content":"speaking of hormones what is the effect of the one that merely block puberty?<br /> <br /> after all it can't that they block all the effects of puberty else children who started taking them at the age of 12 would be very short right?<br /> <br /> for instance consider model andreja pejic. before her transition her body was, for all intents and purposes that of a skinny male. yet she had been taking them for years.<br /> the only effects i could see is tha(according to what she said) she never grew any facial hair and perhaps she had the slightiest hing of breasts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:57:16-07:00","id":952688,"title":"","content":"I do not know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:11:28-07:00","id":952697,"title":"","content":"I'm not really aware of hormones that block puberty. I know that kids who go on hormones before puberty tend to have a much easier transition than those who go on HRT later in life, because it basically changes the way puberty affects them the first time, rather than having to go through a second puberty. I haven't personally known anyone who has done that though, so I don't really know anything more specific about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:04:09-07:00","id":953217,"title":"","content":"nevermind. i did some research and found it. essentially they do things like preventing facial hair a big adam's apple and preserve the voice &quot;soft&quot;<br /> <br /> i think the reason most people never do it is because you can just go for HRT anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T15:56:26-07:00","id":953461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=908394#post908394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a man I find that insulting, masculinity is a wonderful thing (as is feminity), its not of lesser value then feminity.<br /> <br /> This clearly bothers you not for medical reasons, but because you've been taught that men and maculinity are bad.<br /> <br /> There is more to maculinity then violence, hell feminity can be violent too.<br /> <br /> Maculinity builds cities, cures disease, and all kinds of cool stuff.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong feminity can be awesome as well, and as Pagan I try to cultivate both according what fits me as a man.<br /> <br /> I wish your friend luck, your friend will have unique challenge, but will also have a chance to explore masculinity with fresh eyes. Its a huge opportunity to grow as a person, and be truer to who your friend feels to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a strange and wrong understanding of what masculinity is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:00:47-07:00","id":953489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=953461#post953461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a strange and wrong understanding of what masculinity is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be very interested in hearing you (or anyone else) explain their views of both masculinity and femininity. How do you define &quot;a man&quot; and how do you define &quot;a woman&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:25:36-07:00","id":953503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=953489#post953489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be very interested in hearing you (or anyone else) explain their views of both masculinity and femininity. How do you define &quot;a man&quot; and how do you define &quot;a woman&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, neither is really a thing that exists independent of a culture that defines them. Masculinity is no more or less than the traits, preferences, and behaviors that a culture attributes to men, and femininity the same for women. &quot;Man&quot; and &quot;Woman&quot; are socially constructed identifiers that give context to the concepts of masculinity and femininity. Each individual has their own unique combination of traits, preferences, and behaviors, some of them considered masculine or feminine by the culture they live in. Often, people find that the gender that the majority of their traits, preferences, and behaviors are culturally associated with is the one they prefer to be identified by. Other times, it's less cut and dried, and they would prefer to be identified a different way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T02:07:17-07:00","id":953724,"title":"","content":"I would view Masculine or Feminine as cultural traits, but where the definition of man or woman has some different details they are more or less universal.<br /> <br /> Not speaking for anyone but myself here: I do not merely identify as female. I am female. It is intrinsic and inseparable from who I am. I identify as a Goth. It affects how I dress, how I make up, and impacts my interests. I identify as a Gamer. I identify as a Kinkster and a Bohemian. But I could turn my back on those things. I cannot turn my back on being female. God knows, I tried, It left me damaged. My femaleness is intrinsic. I chose to be a Goth, because I like a lot of things about it. I chose to be gamer because I enjoy it. I did not choose my being female.<br /> <br /> In that vein, I don't merely identify as a lesbian, I am one. In a culture or world isolated from western culture, I would still be attracted to women, just as I would be one, regardless of the body I am in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T03:22:25-07:00","id":953738,"title":"","content":"I think Masculine and Feminine are cultural, but man or woman (or some other gender or lack thereof) is internal and just part of you. That said, what someone says (and believes, but I'm going to generally assume they're telling the truth) is what their gender is. It's pretty simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T20:00:20-07:00","id":954161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=948717#post948717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently doing a bit of research on gender transition (for writing, not for myself), and I've been trying to figure out how long it would take on average to undergo a full physical transition. I've seen claims of two years, five, close to ten and anywhere in between. How long does a physical transition roughly take, given that everything goes well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey,I'm trans too, I'll see if I can help.<br /> <br /> It takes as long as you make it but for the sake of your own sanity, understand that things like hormones take time. A lot of time. In cisgender women puberty takes a decade. You'll see results you might be satisfied with before that though. I've been on estrogen and spiro for a bit more than a year and I'm just starting to see boobs. Some ladies get big ones really quickly and some stay flat for a while.<br /> <br /> SRS costs as much as a house. You can expect it to be a pain in the ass to find a competent surgeon (and you want a competent surgeon if you're going to get SRS) and may even have to grab your pass port and go to Thailand or Korea or some place else to find one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T21:17:44-07:00","id":954187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=953489#post953489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be very interested in hearing you (or anyone else) explain their views of both masculinity and femininity. How do you define &quot;a man&quot; and how do you define &quot;a woman&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a hard one. I've been trapped with this question by a trans hater who is convinced that I have a mental illness, that I'm going against nature, blah blah blah.<br /> <br /> The truth is that gender variant people and trans people show that there is more complication to the matter. The truth is that I have no idea what makes a man a man or a woman a woman because I can't possibly, as just one person define it for everyone. Its some cultural thing that I can't grasp. All I can say is that for me, masculinity isn't me. It's not what I see myself as. I am a woman. I always was. And that is what is my home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T21:56:36-07:00","id":954205,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone, I suppose I'm a bit late but I'd like to throw my hat into the ring here. I'm agender, and I'm not really out about it to anyone. Mainly because my gender (or lack of it, depending on how you look at it) doesn't come up much.<br /> <br /> Now I have a question, that is largely philosophical and mainly to help me with a discussion in a group I'm involved with. The question is whether agender people should be considered transgender. Obviously, agender people fall under the trans umbrella, but for myself I don't consider myself being trans because I have no intention to transition. I understand I don't speak for all agender people, I'm just interested in hearing what others have to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:16:24-07:00","id":954219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dman1123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954205#post954205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone, I suppose I'm a bit late but I'd like to throw my hat into the ring here. I'm agender, and I'm not really out about it to anyone. Mainly because my gender (or lack of it, depending on how you look at it) doesn't come up much.<br /> <br /> Now I have a question, that is largely philosophical and mainly to help me with a discussion in a group I'm involved with. The question is whether agender people should be considered transgender. Obviously, agender people fall under the trans umbrella, but for myself I don't consider myself being trans because I have no intention to transition. I understand I don't speak for all agender people, I'm just interested in hearing what others have to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to transition, or even intend to transition, to be trans. Trans isn't short for transition, transition and transgender just both use the same Latin prefix, which literally means across from, beyond, or through. So, yes, agender is part of the transgender spectrum. That said, if you don't consider transness to be an important part of your identity, that's perfectly valid. But, if you did want to be considered trans you would have every right to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:16:37-07:00","id":954220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dman1123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954205#post954205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone, I suppose I'm a bit late but I'd like to throw my hat into the ring here. I'm agender, and I'm not really out about it to anyone. Mainly because my gender (or lack of it, depending on how you look at it) doesn't come up much.<br /> <br /> Now I have a question, that is largely philosophical and mainly to help me with a discussion in a group I'm involved with. The question is whether agender people should be considered transgender. Obviously, agender people fall under the trans umbrella, but for myself I don't consider myself being trans because I have no intention to transition. I understand I don't speak for all agender people, I'm just interested in hearing what others have to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think that transgender identities specifically relate to individuals with dysphoria, who struggle with presentation and perception of gender. Agender people are certainly under the queer umbrella, but I'm not sure if I would personally consider them trans because there's no transition involved.<br /> <br /> But then again, I freely admit that I don't truly grasp being agender. I think I'm trans myself and have known quite a few genderfluid/genderqueer individuals, but 'agender' seems to be a non-label to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:23:05-07:00","id":954225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954220#post954220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that transgender identities specifically relate to individuals with dysphoria, who struggle with presentation and perception of gender. Agender people are certainly under the queer umbrella, but I'm not sure if I would personally consider them trans because there's no transition involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a trans (genderfluid) person who doesn't typically experience dysphoria and doesn't intend to transition, I can't get behind this definition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954220#post954220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then again, I freely admit that I don't truly grasp being agender. I think I'm trans myself and have known quite a few genderfluid/genderqueer individuals, but 'agender' seems to be a non-label to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it you can empathize with feelings of dysphoria? Imagine feeling dysphoria not just for the gender you were assigned at birth, but for any gender. That's how my partner's sibling who is agender describes it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:37:38-07:00","id":954230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954220#post954220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agender people are certainly under the queer umbrella, but I'm not sure if I would personally consider them trans because there's no transition involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my thought as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:38:54-07:00","id":954231,"title":"","content":"That's not what trans means, though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:46:24-07:00","id":954234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954225#post954225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a trans (genderfluid) person who doesn't typically experience dysphoria and doesn't intend to transition, I can't get behind this definition.<br /> <br /> <br /> I take it you can empathize with feelings of dysphoria? Imagine feeling dysphoria not just for the gender you were assigned at birth, but for any gender. That's how my partner's sibling who is agender describes it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Most of the individuals I've personally known who have defined themselves as agender have been less &quot;I'm uncomfortable with any notion of being gendered&quot; and rather &quot;I've opted out of the whole gender thing entirely.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T00:13:39-07:00","id":954256,"title":"","content":"I would generally consider agender somewhere on the trans spectrum as a thought process, but someone could consider themselves agender and not trans, or consider agender a big part of their identity and trans small. The biggest question for me is do they have access to appropriate spaces and resources? If an agender person did not consider themselves trans thus had no desire for trans resources or spaces, that's not a problem. the problem comes if other people say they are not trans and deny an agender person spaces or resources for trans people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:37:41-07:00","id":954315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954234#post954234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Most of the individuals I've personally known who have defined themselves as agender have been less &amp;quot;I'm uncomfortable with any notion of being gendered&amp;quot; and rather &amp;quot;I've opted out of the whole gender thing entirely.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've seen that as well. I actually experimented with that brand of agender for a little while before learning about nonbinary genders, as neither male or female on their own ever quite felt right for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:21:26-07:00","id":954393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dman1123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954205#post954205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone, I suppose I'm a bit late but I'd like to throw my hat into the ring here. I'm agender, and I'm not really out about it to anyone. Mainly because my gender (or lack of it, depending on how you look at it) doesn't come up much.<br /> <br /> Now I have a question, that is largely philosophical and mainly to help me with a discussion in a group I'm involved with. The question is whether agender people should be considered transgender. Obviously, agender people fall under the trans umbrella, but for myself I don't consider myself being trans because I have no intention to transition. I understand I don't speak for all agender people, I'm just interested in hearing what others have to say.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would only consider agender people transgender if they want to be considered that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:41:48-07:00","id":954485,"title":"","content":"This is probably the stupidest question you folks have ever had in this thread, but is possible for medication to temporarily change your gender identity, because sometimes, when the levels of my current bipolar meds get high enough in my body, I feel more feminine then masculine and even visualize myself female, but I go back to being masculine as the meds wear off, though I go back to masculine quicker if I do something masculine coded.<br /> <br /> Is what I am saying even possible? Keep in mind, I am already having side effects to the meds that my doc says aren't normal side effects, so this could just be a weird way that I personally react to the meds due to my own screwed up body chemistry.<br /> <br /> Also, do you folks have any advice for portraying a trans character before and after their transition in my novel series. Said character first appears after their transition in book two (taking place in late 2012), but the series has two plot lines, one of them being a flashback plot line where the same character appears per-transition during the 90s, but the transition itself doesn't happen during series (since it happened during the 2000s that the series doesn't cover.) Any advice on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-20-2016, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:14:53-07:00","id":954501,"title":"","content":"Maybe? I haven't heard of such a thing happening, but that doesn't mean it isn't possible. I mean, if your medication changes your brain chemistry, it could be that the way you think and feel on the medication coses one gender resonate more strongly with you, and the way you think and feel off the medication causes another to resonate with you better.<br /> <br /> You may also be bigender or gender fluid - the way you feel about gender on the meds or off the meds could both be equally valid and important parts of your identity, which may not conform to one gender, and the meds may just be a catalyst for switching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:37:57-07:00","id":954551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954501#post954501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe? I haven't heard of such a thing happening, but that doesn't mean it isn't possible. I mean, if your medication changes your brain chemistry, it could be that the way you think and feel on the medication coses one gender resonate more strongly with you, and the way you think and feel off the medication causes another to resonate with you better.<br /> <br /> You may also be bigender or gender fluid - the way you feel about gender on the meds or off the meds could both be equally valid and important parts of your identity, which may not conform to one gender, and the meds may just be a catalyst for switching.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds reasonable. I will admit that I have never been the perfect picture of masculinity, so the idea I might be bi-gender or genderfluid makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> It's just that I always saw my rejection of certain aspects of masculinity as a rejection of my father (who would be the picture in the feminist dictionary under toxic masculinity if it weren't for Donald Trump)... I'm gonna have to think about this. Thanks for your input, Charlaquin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:09:08-07:00","id":954567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954485#post954485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably the stupidest question you folks have ever had in this thread, but is possible for medication to temporarily change your gender identity, because sometimes, when the levels of my current bipolar meds get high enough in my body, I feel more feminine then masculine and even visualize myself female, but I go back to being masculine as the meds wear off, though I go back to masculine quicker if I do something masculine coded.<br /> <br /> Is what I am saying even possible? Keep in mind, I am already having side effects to the meds that my doc says aren't normal side effects, so this could just be a weird way that I personally react to the meds due to my own screwed up body chemistry.<br /> <br /> Also, do you folks have any advice for portraying a trans character before and after their transition in my novel series. Said character first appears after their transition in book two (taking place in late 2012), but the series has two plot lines, one of them being a flashback plot line where the same character appears per-transition during the 90s, but the transition itself doesn't happen during series (since it happened during the 2000s that the series doesn't cover.) Any advice on that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've heard this is similar to the experience of bigender people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:16:34-07:00","id":954609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954551#post954551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds reasonable. I will admit that I have never been the perfect picture of masculinity, so the idea I might be bi-gender or genderfluid makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> It's just that I always saw my rejection of certain aspects of masculinity as a rejection of my father (who would be the picture in the feminist dictionary under toxic masculinity if it weren't for Donald Trump)... I'm gonna have to think about this. Thanks for your input, Charlaquin.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. Being genderfluid myself, I can definitely understand the feeling of identifying with different blends of masculinity and femininity at different times, though for me it isn't a switch between distinct states so much as a constant flux. My partner is bigender though, and does have two distinct genders they switch between. So what you're describing is definitely not unheard of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T01:03:22-07:00","id":954879,"title":"","content":"Not that I am aware of, but this is an area which there is sadly little research","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:38:25-07:00","id":955091,"title":"","content":"I'm going to say probably. But, more in that it offers a different perspective and brain chemistry to boot. Frankly, I can't exactly say I know that change of mind, in spite of being both trans and having pretty severe bipolar. But based off my experiences, I think it's not unlikely. Hell, I can seem like completely different people depending on where my mood is at. So feeling a different gender is something I could see. The problem is, this sort of thing (among many others) isn't really researched like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar56_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"56\" data-vbnamecard=\"56\">Baroness Nerak</a> said. I mean, it basically was only fairly recently that a lot of disorders were even considered to be something children could have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T07:11:19-07:00","id":955557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OrionTyson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=954567#post954567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've heard this is similar to the experience of bigender people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:56:00-07:00","id":955908,"title":"","content":"Very well then I might be Bi-gender... Is it weird that the name I imagine for my female side is nothing like my real name? I think of my female self as being named &quot;Alana Harper&quot; which would translate as &quot;Tree Harp Player&quot; according to google. I have no idea why that name pops up in my head either? Is that a thing with bi-gender people, that you automatically know the name your non-birth side has?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:32:15-07:00","id":956014,"title":"","content":"I can't speak for bi-gendered, but for me discovering myself as a female I sort of struggled with my name. Well, mostly between three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:35:20-07:00","id":956016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=956014#post956014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for bi-gendered, but for me discovering myself as a female I sort of struggled with my name. Well, mostly between three.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I guess I am just lucky to already know the name. The name Alana Harper (to be fair, I am not certain on the spelling of Alana, I have the sound in my head but not the word itself) just speaks to me some how.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:28:52-07:00","id":956050,"title":"","content":"Which is cool. Please don't take my words as skepticism or anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T19:02:31-07:00","id":956067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=956014#post956014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for bi-gendered, but for me discovering myself as a female I sort of struggled with my name. Well, mostly between three.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, I grew up with one name, used another for over a decade, and then publicly renounced it as a symbolic way of destroying my past self while going back to my earlier one. That masculine Davis is the name I buried and the delightfully archaic (and somewhat more gender neutral) Lex is the one I use is probably just a coincidence, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T05:42:14-07:00","id":956276,"title":"","content":"I think finding a name isn't generally the easiest thing, and frankly, the name that suits you NOW, might not be the one that suits you a year or ten down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:21:51-07:00","id":956487,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Whenever anyone asks me what name I want to be called, I just say &quot;Gecko&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T17:37:25-07:00","id":956650,"title":"","content":"I've gone by a few different names, with my friends. Right now, I use &quot;Glitter&quot; a lot. It started as a joke, but now I answer to it almost as easily as my birth name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:37:05-07:00","id":957263,"title":"","content":"I'm such a dork I named myself after a character from my favorite game series. I named myself Terra, after the character from Final Fantasy VI. I thought it was a pretty name but not silly sounding and I just felt like it was a good fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:39:39-07:00","id":957395,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input all you folks.<br /> <br /> I just want to point out that my masculine side is still more or less dominant, in that it's the side I identify with most of the time, but when my brain chemistry flips to feminine, I am very much feminine. So... I guess I am bi-gender leaning toward male? Do bi-gender people sometimes lean toward one or the other, is that normal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:47:02-07:00","id":957397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=957395#post957395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the input all you folks.<br /> <br /> I just want to point out that my masculine side is still more or less dominant, in that it's the side I identify with most of the time, but when my brain chemistry flips to feminine, I am very much feminine. So... I guess I am bi-gender leaning toward male? Do bi-gender people sometimes lean toward one or the other, is that normal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. My partner is bigender and is distinctly female most of the time, goes by their birth name and she/her/hers pronouns. Occasionally they have days where they prefer a different name and he/him/his pronouns (though consider themselves nonbinary on those days rather than distinctly male), and lean pretty feminine in either case. Despite the name, bigender doesn't have to mean your genders fall within the binary, nor that you have to have exactly two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:43:33-07:00","id":957470,"title":"","content":"I just have to say that I'm mindblown. Especially by the different names thing. Is that important? Obviously it is, if several people are doing it, but I never found my name as a big part of identity of what/how I am. It's just a thing people address me with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T02:15:11-07:00","id":957479,"title":"","content":"For me it wasn't till it was. I needed a more feminine name once I was full time. Now I picked something similar to both my birth name and what I am called online. But until I was full time not strongly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:37:37-07:00","id":957615,"title":"","content":"I also just realized that some names have a gender &quot;assigned to them&quot;, so when shifting between them a different gender name makes sense. Or a gender neutral name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:01:37-07:00","id":957834,"title":"","content":"Depends on how gendered you are. I know women, trans and cis, who like &quot;Alex&quot; or &quot;Lex&quot; because it is androgynous. I intensely wanted a feminine name when the time came. I want no chance of an innocent mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:15:09-07:00","id":957872,"title":"","content":"My name has never been a big thing for me. Not that I wouldn't like a more feminine name, but nothing I've tried has really felt right, and I'm not bothered by the name my friends have called me by since before I knew I was genderfluid. Though, I've found myself rather liking when folks around here call me Charley. It's just the right amount of gender neutral to suit me no matter how I'm feeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T17:51:03-07:00","id":957957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=957834#post957834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how gendered you are. I know women, trans and cis, who like &amp;quot;Alex&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Lex&amp;quot; because it is androgynous. I intensely wanted a feminine name when the time came. I want no chance of an innocent mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Lex because it's always been my name; it being gender-ambiguous and having a Latin meaning are unexpected benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:08:30-07:00","id":958375,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of Glitter because it is fairly ambiguous, plus it's a perfect representation of my personality. Loud, colorful, and all over the place that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:24:28-07:00","id":958503,"title":"","content":"So, I have a question and I am kind of afraid to ask, because I don't want to come off as trivial but I do want to ask the trans members of this board a question.<br /> <br /> If one were writing a character who is transgendered, whether for a written story, or even just something like a fanfic or an RPG character, how would one go about that without offending anyone? I ask because I am brainstorming ideas for a nWoD fanfic and one of the main characters is trans, specifically a character who transitioned from male to female in her early teens (she is in her mid-twenties when the story takes place). The issue is that I am a cisgendered male and I'm worried I may get things wrong about the struggle that trans people go through. I know I should make the character well-rounded and have depth to her beyond her gender, that is obvious. But I am worried that I may get something wrong and accidentally offend people.<br /> <br /> I know my question probably seems trivial and I don't want to come across as trivializing the issues that the trans community faces, but I figured I'd ask the question and get answers from my fellow RPG fans, particularly those in the LGBT community. I myself am LGBT, being bisexual and all, but I don't have much experience with trans issues, particularly Male-to-Female transgendered individuals. I do have some friends who are Female-to-Male transgendered, one of whom is my best friend in real life and is somewhat closested about his experience (as such I will not mention his name).<br /> <br /> So, I hope I didn't upset anyone with my question and I would love to hear some advice in writing a transgender character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:53:56-07:00","id":958526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=958503#post958503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a question and I am kind of afraid to ask, because I don't want to come off as trivial but I do want to ask the trans members of this board a question.<br /> <br /> If one were writing a character who is transgendered, whether for a written story, or even just something like a fanfic or an RPG character, how would one go about that without offending anyone? I ask because I am brainstorming ideas for a nWoD fanfic and one of the main characters is trans, specifically a character who transitioned from male to female in her early teens (she is in her mid-twenties when the story takes place). The issue is that I am a cisgendered male and I'm worried I may get things wrong about the struggle that trans people go through. I know I should make the character well-rounded and have depth to her beyond her gender, that is obvious. But I am worried that I may get something wrong and accidentally offend people.<br /> <br /> I know my question probably seems trivial and I don't want to come across as trivializing the issues that the trans community faces, but I figured I'd ask the question and get answers from my fellow RPG fans, particularly those in the LGBT community. I myself am LGBT, being bisexual and all, but I don't have much experience with trans issues, particularly Male-to-Female transgendered individuals. I do have some friends who are Female-to-Male transgendered, one of whom is my best friend in real life and is somewhat closested about his experience (as such I will not mention his name).<br /> <br /> So, I hope I didn't upset anyone with my question and I would love to hear some advice in writing a transgender character.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, a minor nitpick: it's transgender, not transgendered.<br /> <br /> As for the main bulk of your question, I have to wonder how it impacts the narrative? Someone who is trans is so much more than that as a person and especially if this character transitioned a decade ago, I'm not sure what there is to mention and possibly screw up. If there's a general pitfall I'd suggest avoiding, don't make her character a vessel for sadness porn (i.e. constantly lamenting how she was born in the wrong body or internally monologuing about her gender) and don't take the route of the awful Dragon Age comics (where a notable transwoman character is tossed into jail and we're treated to several pages of her dress torn off to reveal a flat, masculine chest as the &quot;big reveal&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T04:10:53-07:00","id":958677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=958526#post958526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, a minor nitpick: it's transgender, not transgendered.<br /> <br /> As for the main bulk of your question, I have to wonder how it impacts the narrative? Someone who is trans is so much more than that as a person and especially if this character transitioned a decade ago, I'm not sure what there is to mention and possibly screw up. If there's a general pitfall I'd suggest avoiding, don't make her character a vessel for sadness porn (i.e. constantly lamenting how she was born in the wrong body or internally monologuing about her gender) and don't take the route of the awful Dragon Age comics (where a notable transwoman character is tossed into jail and we're treated to several pages of her dress torn off to reveal a flat, masculine chest as the &quot;big reveal&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I am sorry for my terminology mishap. Again, I am not too good with these things. And as for your advice, I will do my best to avoid those pitfalls. Thank you for the advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:18:55-07:00","id":958715,"title":"","content":"It's cool. This is a place to ask questions, so you have a bit more leeway here than perhaps otherwise.<br /> <br /> To some degree, I do agree with atamajakki, don't make them sadness porn. The simplist thing is treat them like anyone else; I mean, if their being transgender is not really relevant it may not come up, though they still are. Or it can be referenced offhandedly through description, or another character making a concerned comment. I would recommend against that being a main plot point without research; I mean it is easy to write a group of women and one is trans. Making a story focusing on that is harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:22:51-07:00","id":958716,"title":"","content":"Definitely avoid the &quot;shocking reveal&quot;, in any form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T07:03:19-07:00","id":958724,"title":"","content":"To my part, you could focus on things that being transgender gave them. Sure, it's not easy and whatnot... but as this thread (and others) show, there's a sense of community and attempts to be supportive and understanding. Maybe this is just me, but it seems like a fairly large number I've known had activist tendancies of some sort. But above all, just treat them as a person, and if there's a &quot;reveal&quot;, it should just be them talking about it with someone they trust with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T07:03:33-07:00","id":958725,"title":"","content":"Hi. I am generally content with my life, but there are times (like when I read this thread) I feel gnawings of discontent. I envy London Fog from Aberrant Worldwide Phase II. She got to turn into a woman in one fell swoop, no surgery, no awkwardness, and she got superpowers too.<br /> <br /> I had boyfriends in high school and college, but I dated women too. One girlfriend in college told me when we were arguing that I had a personality she had only seen in some women. I felt immensely flattered because she recognized that I was female underneath.<br /> <br /> My name comes from the Roman emperor Julian, the last pagan emperor and (possibly) a transgender person. I have several girlfriends (people I date) but none of them know this side of me. I am a corporate lawyer with a Big Four accounting firm, and the culture at my job is not very accepting of LGBT lifestyles.<br /> <br /> Thank you for listening.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen (my name if I'd been born a girl)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:20:47-07:00","id":958887,"title":"","content":"Nice to meet you Colleen. Are you looking for advice of any sort or just want to introduce yourself? Either is fine, of course","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:25:15-07:00","id":959200,"title":"","content":"Baroness,<br /> <br /> LOVE your Golden Eagle chronicle! The Twenties/Thirties/Forties is one of my favorite time periods. I just want to be able to talk with other trans people, to be reassured that my feelings are valid and I'm not just being silly or flighty. I'm afraid if I tell people I like the truth, they won't find me attractive anymore, and my whole identity is based on being desirable.<br /> <br /> This is a verse from my favorite song, &quot;Wildwood Flower&quot;:<br /> <br /> I will twine with my mingles of raven-black hair<br /> With the roses so red and the lilies so fair<br /> With the myrtle so bright with its emerald hue<br /> And the pale and the leader with eyes look so blue<br /> <br /> Take care. Thanks again for listening.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T10:10:40-07:00","id":961103,"title":"","content":"I do have a question, but it is hard to couch. I know what gender is intellectually and as a term, but I guess I don't know what it specifically is. I mean what is femininity? That question often bothers me. I have always identified as a woman but always failed to be feminine and I guess that seems like it has to be an oxymoron? Gender being a cultural association; what is it to be a feminine man or a masculine woman? I mean with femininity as womanhood can someone be much more feminine than masculine even extremely so and still be a man? Can someone associate with the identity of an opposite gender (not meaning sex, but identifying as a gender they do not in any way exemplify but seem to identify with anyway) I very much apologize if this is in any way insulting, but it's something that's been bothering me for a while and I am having trouble finding answers elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:13:08-07:00","id":961154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/786516-trans-q-a-thread?p=961103#post961103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a question, but it is hard to couch. I know what gender is intellectually and as a term, but I guess I don't know what it specifically is. I mean what is femininity? That question often bothers me. I have always identified as a woman but always failed to be feminine and I guess that seems like it has to be an oxymoron? Gender being a cultural association; what is it to be a feminine man or a masculine woman? I mean with femininity as womanhood can someone be much more feminine than masculine even extremely so and still be a man? Can someone associate with the identity of an opposite gender (not meaning sex, but identifying as a gender they do not in any way exemplify but seem to identify with anyway) I very much apologize if this is in any way insulting, but it's something that's been bothering me for a while and I am having trouble finding answers elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gender is self identification. Now what you (seem by how I read it) are talking is gender performance or presentation, which is different. I think it's a fair question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:10:13-07:00","id":961191,"title":"","content":"I forget if I've posted this before, but I've found this infographic often helps people. It's not perfect (there have been at least three versions made, as understanding of gender issues develops), but it's still a useful tool for explaining the concepts to more visual learners.<br /> <img src=\"http://itspronouncedmetrosexual.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/Genderbread-Person-3.3.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> To answer the question more directly, yes, it's entirely possible for men to be feminine and women to be masculine. This is true of cis people and trans people. You may be the most hyper-masculine person you know and like it that way, but still feel that you are a woman and would rather be recognized as such, that doesn't make you any less of a woman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-31-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}